/MEM accepts the result eight cycles after capture when ready. During the wait, ID/EX and fetch hold while older instructions drain and EX/MEM receives bubbles with writeback and memory enables cleared. The result returns through the usual EX/MEM forwarding path. ALTOPS captures the original substitute value at request time and uses the same handshake and latency.\n\nThe divider reuses the dividend shift register to accumulate quotient digits and derives 2D by shifting the registered D. The radix-4 recurrence yields the required divide-by-zero values with quotient negation suppressed. The signed overflow case falls out of the normal 32-bit result selection. Divider vectors moved to a dedicated cocotb runner. The pipeline regression checks that a divide captures a load result across a stalled older store and forwards its quotient immediately to the next instruction.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Verilator `-Wall` lint passed for both the hardware and ALTOPS builds. The guarded include in `core.sv` supports the requested lint glob, which can list `core.sv` before the compilation-unit types.\n- All six cocotb runners passed. Divider coverage includes signed and unsigned corner cases, varied operand widths, consecutive requests, and deferred result acceptance.\n- `bash formal/run_all.sh` passed all 53 single-retirement ALTOPS checks, including liveness, with zero failures and zero fixes. The arithmetic datapath was exercised by cocotb and cosim. The separate `formal-deep` suite was outside this local check.\n- `make cosim TARGET=bench NRET=1` passed selftest and three random traces with and without stalls, plus the canonical stalled CoreMark CRC check. The run reached EBREAK and reported no out-of-bounds accesses.\n\n## Measured fitness\n\n| Metric | Baseline | Shared divider |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| CoreMark cycles between markers | 4,491,485 | 4,491,485 |\n| Median Gowin Fmax | 5.442 MHz | 45.180 MHz |\n| CoreMark iterations/second | 12.12 | 100.59 |\n\nGowin placement options 0, 1, and 2 reported 43.715, 45.180, and 45.180 MHz. Option 0's worst path spans 49 cells through regfile read, redirect, and hazard logic, compared with the baseline's 156-cell worst path through the ALU. Fitness increased 730.2%. The stalled CoreMark trace recorded two DIVU retirements outside the markers and zero DIV or REM family retirements in the measured interval. Divide-heavy workloads pay the eight additional EX cycles per operation.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
