{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_35", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"git log -6 --oneline && rg -n '83\\\\.921' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\"", "aggregated_output": "34e8b51 log: hyp-20261120-003-r8s2 regression\n3faec1d log: hyp-20261120-002-r8s1 improvement\n4ab5c53 log: hyp-20261120-001-r8s0 regression\ncc084f3 hyp-20261120-002-r8s1: Pipeline instruction replay ahead of the fetch queue (+12.4%)\naee4eb1 log: hyp-20261120-003-r7s2 improvement\n4331e9f log: hyp-20261120-002-r7s1 regression\n24:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261120-002-r8s1\", \"title\": \"Pipeline instruction replay ahead of the fetch queue\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"The bench champion scores 210.96 CoreMark iter/sec at 79.292 MHz over\\n3,758,572 marked cycles. Its learned stream table only opens replay\\nafter a BTB hit, and a replayed word must enter the FIFO before decode\\ncan use it. Profiling found about 272,000 cycles where the issue queue\\nwas empty and no external instruction word was ready. A separate\\nsynchronous replay lookup one cycle ahead of the fetch queue can cover\\nmore of those cycles and take the bulk of the replay storage out of LUT RAM.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The bench champion scores 210.96 CoreMark iter/sec at 79.292 MHz over\\n3,758,572 marked cycles. Its learned stream table only opens replay\\nafter a BTB hit, and a replayed word must enter the FIFO before decode\\ncan use it. Profiling found about 272,000 cycles where the issue queue\\nwas empty and no external instruction word was ready. A separate\\nsynchronous replay lookup one cycle ahead of the fetch queue can cover\\nmore of those cycles and take the bulk of the replay storage out of LUT RAM.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Replace the stream-relative replay stage with a synchronous block-RAM\\nlookup keyed by the fetch PC. Start with 512 entries containing an\\ninstruction word, the full remaining PC tag, and a valid bit. Whenever\\nfetch accepts the current word, use the same predicted successor that\\nupdates the fetch PC to read the next replay entry on that edge. Hold\\nthe RAM output and its collision metadata when fetch holds. The ready\\nexternal response and registered replay result become two producers of\\nthe existing fall-through FIFO. A r\n…[3060 of 6132 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:ace3a36b10220eba]…\n\"fitness\": 237.06, \"delta_pct\": 12.37, \"vs_baseline\": 1855.94, \"fmax_mhz\": 83.921, \"ipc_coremark\": 3e-06, \"cycles\": 3540112, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 5410, \"ff\": 1078, \"seeds\": [77.808, 83.921, 83.921], \"perturbations\": [[0, 77.808, 11], [1, 83.921, 12], [2, 83.921, 12]], \"lutram\": 104, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 5, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_if/take_target_q_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_if/replay_replay_0_1_s\", \"slack_ns\": -7.852, \"arrival_ns\": 18.147, \"logic_cells\": 28, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_if\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 11, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-20T09:59:34.475451Z\", \"slot\": 1, \"round_id\": 8, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-002-r8s1 (improvement, +12.37%): Reading tagged replay BRAM at the predicted next PC on each fetch advance lets replay hits bypass an empty FIFO during CoreMark instruction-bus stalls even between BTB hits, while a registered FIFO head PC and carry-save JALR comparison shorten the EX successor check.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
