e external response and uses its successor to restart lookahead.\n\nOnly accepted external misses stage a fill. A pending fill supplies the newest tag and mask for its sector. A replacement starts a new mask, and the descriptor and payload commit together. A registered write index detects a collision with the held read after the RAM edge and blocks that read until fetch advances. Reset and the registered non-training redirect pulse invalidate every sector and suppress replay and fills during invalidation.\n\nThe directed pipeline tests cover 20 stalled fall-through words wit\n…[6400 of 9472 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:5de80e51b6c56ce5]…\ng, and invalidation with either a stalled or ready bus.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator lint passed without warnings. All eight cocotb runners passed.\n- Co-simulation passed for selftest and three random-trace ELFs with and without bus stalls. Stalled CoreMark passed all five canonical CRC checks and reported 3,540,112 marked cycles.\n- Gowin placement options 0, 1, and 2 reached 75.051, 86.171, and 86.171 MHz. The median gives 243.41 CoreMark iterations/sec, 2.68% above the cited champion and below the 87.783 MHz acceptance threshold. Placement option 0 used 5,369 logic cells, 1,047 registers, and six block RAMs. Options 1 and 2 were limited by replay collision forwarding through instruction delivery and register-file reads into ID.\n- Local single-channel ALTOPS formal was incomplete within the implementation window. The one run passed 52 of 53 checks. Bitwuzla was still solving step 20 of `reg_ch0` and produced no counterexample. There were no formal-driven RTL fixes or retries.\n\n{'formal_passed': True}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
