{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_40", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n '\"'^'\"\\\\[|program|MUL' formal/checks-deep.cfg | head -35 && sed -n '1,95p' formal/checks-deep.cfg && sed -n '1,120p' tools/eval/_slots.py && du -sh \\\"\"'$TMPDIR\"/bench-mul-*'", "aggregated_output": "1:[options]\n6:[depth]\n24:[defines]\n34:#   ✗ does NOT prove: the actual MUL/DIV/REM arithmetic is correct.\n40:#   2. cosim against test/cosim/reference.py — every retired MUL/DIV/REM\n46:[cover]\n52:[verilog-files]\n[options]\nisa rv32im\nnret 1\nsolver bitwuzla\n\n[depth]\n# BMC depth per check. 2nd column (where present) is the k-induction prove\n# depth. Keep depths matched to the current pipeline so bugs within ~20\n# cycles of any symbolic instruction stream are exposed.\ninsn          20\nreg       10  20\npc_fwd    10  20\npc_bwd    10  20\ncausal    10  20\n# unique   — no two retirements share rvfi_order (catches double-retire)\n# cover    — sanity that the CPU retires (prevents vacuous-pass suites)\n# ill      — illegal instructions must trap; rvfi_trap from decoder.is_illegal\n# liveness — CPU makes forward progress under any symbolic stream\nunique     1 10 20\ncover      1    20\nill             20\nliveness   1 10 20\n\n[defines]\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALIGNED_MEM\n# RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS — fast mode. Substitutes M-ext mul/div/rem with\n# simpler XOR-of-add/sub formulas so bitwuzla solves them inside the\n# 20-step BMC budget (rvfi.rst §7.6 \"Alternative arithmetic operations\").\n#\n# IMPORTANT — what this DOES and DOES NOT prove:\n#   ✓ proves: M-ext bypassing, operand routing (rs1/rs2 -> unit -> rd),\n#             stall/forwarding behavior on mul/div, all I-base arithmetic\n#             and trap discipline.\n#   ✗ does NOT prove: the actual MUL/DIV/REM arithmetic is correct.\n#     The DUT and the spec both implement the same XOR substitute under\n#     this define, so a wrong real multiplier can still pass formal here.\n#\n# M-extension arithmetic correctness is covered separately by:\n#   1. test/test_alu.py — 30+ vectors per M-ext op, exact bit results.\n#   2. cosim against test/cosim/reference.py — every retired MUL/DIV/REM\n#      diff'd field-by-field.\n#   3. `make formal-deep` — same checks without ALTOPS. SLOW (~hours per\n#      M-ext check) but proves real arithmetic. Run periodically, not in\n#      the per-iteration orchestrator lo\n…[2119 of 5191 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:57e527d4b0772f17]…\n          f.close()\n                continue\n            waited = time.time() - started\n            if waited > 60:\n                print(f\"  [eval] {what}: got host eval slot {i} after {waited:.0f}s\", flush=True)\n            try:\n                yield\n            finally:\n                fcntl.flock(f, fcntl.LOCK_UN)\n                f.close()\n            return\n        if not told:\n            print(f\"  [eval] {what}: waiting for a host eval slot ({n} busy)\", flush=True)\n            told = True\n        time.sleep(5)\n\n\ndef eval_jobs(default: str | None = None) -> str | None:\n    \"\"\"make -j for a formal run holding a slot (HARNESS_EVAL_JOBS).\"\"\"\n    return os.environ.get(\"HARNESS_EVAL_JOBS\") or default\n3.9M\t/srv/hwebench/tmp/4876824c/dbcda3ac/bench-mul-cosim\n4.0K\t/srv/hwebench/tmp/4876824c/dbcda3ac/bench-mul-cosim.output\n435M\t/srv/hwebench/tmp/4876824c/dbcda3ac/bench-mul-formal\n256K\t/srv/hwebench/tmp/4876824c/dbcda3ac/bench-mul-formal-fix.output\n260K\t/srv/hwebench/tmp/4876824c/dbcda3ac/bench-mul-formal.output\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
