{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_90","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"stat -c '%n %w' .agent.log .agent.last .git implementation_notes.md && sed -n '1,35p' implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":".agent.log 2026-11-20 06:46:36.348938242 +0100\n.agent.last 2026-11-20 06:46:36.536941650 +0100\n.git 2026-11-20 06:46:36.318383423 +0100\nimplementation_notes.md 2026-11-20 06:54:58.205035620 +0100\n# Bench fetch queue and registered recovery\n\n- IF uses a four-entry fall-through queue with wrap-bit pointers and asynchronous read, synchronous write storage. Each 64-bit word holds the full PC and instruction. Decode issues the head during imem stalls. IF can accept a replacement response on the same edge that decode pops a full queue.\n- EX compares the resolved successor against the oldest unissued PC, using the fetch address when the queue is empty. IF registers both candidates and the resolved select, then uses the selected address and paired EX PC for the predictor write one edge later. The existing tagged last-successor predictor still trains on conditional fall-through.\n- Redirects clear both queue pointers and annul the younger ID/EX slot. IF tracks acceptance of the target response separately from issue of the corrected instruction. FENCE.I uses the same recovery at PC+4. The EX alignment checks and the single-channel RVFI and dmem interfaces follow the existing contract.\n- Recovery registers store aligned word addresses. EX compares full byte addresses and checks target alignment before choosing the recovery candidate. The queue uses an explicit packed bit-vector memory declaration for consistent Yosys and Gowin inference.\n- Updated the two recovery traces to require fetch runahead during dmem holds. Added directed tests for full pop and refill, draining during imem backpressure, redirecting from a full queue, and refetching code modified by a stalled store before FENCE.I.\n\n## Local checks\n\n- Verilator lint, all 84 cocotb cases across seven runners, and `make cosim TARGET=bench NRET=1` passed. Selftest and the three random programs matched the ISS with and without stalls. Stalled CoreMark validated the canonical CRCs (`e9f5`, `e714`, `1fd7`, `8e3a`, `fcaf`) in 4,015,275 marked cycles with no out-of-bounds access.\n- Gowin placed the final RTL at 75.075, 77.436, and 77.436 MHz. The 77.436 MHz median and measured cycle count give 192.85 iterations/s, 12.4% above the champion. Option 0 used 5,049 logic cells and its longest reported path reached the IF recovery register from EX. Options 1 and 2 were divider-limited.\n- Formal passed 52 of 53 checks on the retry while `reg_ch0` is still running. The first `pc_fwd_ch0` counterexample retired a buffered instruction at PC 0 after its predecessor reported 0x14 as the successor. Yosys had lowered the packed-struct array incorrectly. The explicit vector memory fixed the failure and `pc_fwd_ch0` passed on the retry.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
