\": {\"motivation\": \"The bench champion scores 138.16 CoreMark iterations per second at\\n59.595 MHz in 4,313,521 marked cycles. In its median Gowin placement,\\ntwo worst paths reach data BRAM from the register-file BRAM through\\nthe EX operand and ALU muxes. A WB destination-to-data-BRAM path is\\nwithin 0.02 ns of the worst arrival. Both the register-file read a\n…[6939 of 10011 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:2f81d57f2a7b938b]…\ntch `core.yaml`.\\n- The three Gowin placements reached 63.858, 66.149, and 66.149 MHz. The build reports 4,272 LUT4s, 784 registers, 88 LUT-RAM cells, and four BRAMs. The register file uses 32 of the RAM16SDP4 cells, covering both copies of each bank.\\n- CoreMark validated all five canonical CRCs in 4,313,521 marked cycles. The 66.149 MHz median exceeds the 62.34 MHz acceptance margin and yields 153.35 iterations/s, up 11.00% from 138.16 iterations/s.\\n- Single-retire ALTOPS formal passed all 53 checks on the final RTL with zero failures and no corrective retries.\\n\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-20T04:29:51.372280Z\", \"slot\": 0, \"round_id\": 4, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-001-r4s0 (improvement, +10.99%): With asynchronous LUT RAM reads and bypass matches latched at ID/EX, forwarding still appeared among Gowin's worst paths until folding the AUIPC PC and immediate selects into one-hot operand masks removed the serial EX mux, raising median Fmax from 59.994 to 66.149 MHz with unchanged CoreMark cycle count.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
