{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_38", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 -c 'import json; rows=[json.loads(l) for l in open(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\\\")]; [(print(d.get(\\\"id\\\"), d.get(\\\"fitness\\\"),d.get(\\\"cycles\\\"),d.get(\\\"fmax_mhz\\\"),d.get(\\\"seeds\\\"),d.get(\\\"critical_path\\\")), print(d.get(\\\"implementation_notes\\\",\\\"\\\") if d.get(\\\"id\\\",\\\"\\\").endswith(\\\"r7s0\\\") else \\\"\\\")) for d in rows if \\\"-r7s\\\" in d.get(\\\"id\\\",\\\"\\\") ]'\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261120-001-r7s0 203.83 4015275 81.844 [82.894, 81.844, 81.844] {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_4_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_if/read_ptr_q_0_s2', 'slack_ns': -7.064, 'arrival_ns': 17.358, 'logic_cells': 37, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu', 'cpu/u_if']}\n# Bench RTL implementation\n\nID/EX now captures the one-hot raw forwarding masks, the ALU's PC and immediate operand masks, and the integer result enables. EX qualifies its producer tag with the live slot's write intent and JAL/JALR alignment. MEM qualifies its tag after checking load alignment. The younger EX producer has priority. The masks hold with ID/EX during stalls, and the MEM/WB payload remains available during a data bus hold.\n\nEX shares the one-hot integer datapath with the standalone encoded ALU and ORs the enabled integer result with the link and M results. JALR uses the forwarded address sum for alignment. JAL and branches use immediate bit 1 because fetch PCs are word-aligned and relative displacements are even. EX uses the full 32-bit successor comparison to redirect on the existing edge, and MEM/WB provides single-channel retirement.\n\nThe divider captures the first nibble's quotient and remainder and the byte cutoff at launch. It computes the top dividend digit from the raw sign and the low-28-bit zero test, in parallel with the lower magnitude bits. The signed divisor cutoff checks exclude exact magnitudes 16 and 256. The first work edge consumes the second nibble, with the same eight-edge result transfer and ALTOPS formulas.\n\nThe one-hot datapath lives alongside the encoded ALU in `alu.sv`, so existing standalone source lists still work. The final timing pass moved the add and subtract terms to the end of the result OR, simplified EX forwarding qualification using the decoder's write intent, and packed the first quotient nibble into the dividend/quotient register above the unconsumed magnitude bits. The first remainder nibble has its own register.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Verilator lint passed with `-Wall` in both real arithmetic and ALTOPS mode.\n- All 86 cocotb cases passed. Added tests cover trapping JAL, JALR, and LW preserving older writes, signed cutoff and dividend nibble boundaries, and changing divider inputs immediately after capture.\n- SAT proved the actual divider launch magnitude slices, both cutoffs, and first quotient/remainder equivalent to the full-width definitions for symbolic `op`, `a`, and `b`.\n- Selftest and all three random trace programs matched the ISS with no stalls and with both bus stalls. Stalled CoreMark passed canonical CRC validation.\n- The unmodified single-retirement ALTOPS suite passed 52 of 53 checks, including liveness. The depth-20 `reg_ch0` check remained pending at the end of local verification after about 20 minutes in the stock Bitwuzla solver. Supplemental Boolector and BTORMC runs of the same property also remained pending. The runs produced no counterexample and triggered zero RTL fix attempts.\n- Gowin placement options 0, 1, and 2 reached 82.894, 81.844, and 81.844 MHz. The 81.844 MHz median and 4,015,275 marked cycles yield 203.83 CoreMark iterations/s, 5.69% above the champion. Option 0 uses 5,308 logic cells and 993 registers.\n- Timing remains limited by the forwarded JALR address into IF recovery. The measured median is above the acceptance threshold and below the hypothesis's scratch median of 87.108 MHz.\n\nhyp-20261120-002-r7s1 208.89 4015275 83.877 [75.973, 83.877, 83.877] {'from': 'cpu/u_mem/reg_q.ctrl.reg_write_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_if/write_ptr_q_1_s0', 'slack_ns': -8.163, 'arrival_ns': 18.457, 'logic_cells': 37, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu', 'cpu/u_if']}\n\nhyp-20261120-003-r7s2 210.96 3758572 79.292 [79.03, 79.292, 79.292] {'from': 'cpu/u_mem/reg_q.ctrl.reg_write_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_if/recovering_s1', 'slack_ns': -7.653, 'arrival_ns': 17.948, 'logic_cells': 39, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_if', 'cpu/u_ex']}\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
