{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_67","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 -c 'import json; rows=[json.loads(l) for l in open(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\\\")]; [(print(d.get(\\\"id\\\"),d.get(\\\"formal_passed\\\")),print(d.get(\\\"implementation_notes\\\",\\\"\\\"))) for d in rows if d.get(\\\"id\\\",\\\"\\\").endswith(\\\"r7s2\\\")]'; command -v btormc boolector bitwuzla z3; printenv | cut -d= -f1 | rg 'FORMAL|BENCH|GOWIN|TMP'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_67","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 -c 'import json; rows=[json.loads(l) for l in open(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\\\")]; [(print(d.get(\\\"id\\\"),d.get(\\\"formal_passed\\\")),print(d.get(\\\"implementation_notes\\\",\\\"\\\"))) for d in rows if d.get(\\\"id\\\",\\\"\\\").endswith(\\\"r7s2\\\")]'; command -v btormc boolector bitwuzla z3; printenv | cut -d= -f1 | rg 'FORMAL|BENCH|GOWIN|TMP'\"","aggregated_output":"hyp-20261120-003-r7s2 True\n# Learned successor streams\n\nThe bench fetch stage learns 32 streams of up to 16 words. An accepted tagged BTB hit opens the predicted successor stream, including a predicted fall-through. The registered stream row, full tag, and offset drive lookup. A staged fill extends the contiguous prefix only after an accepted external response. Fill admission checks any pending descriptor update for the same row first, while replay uses the committed prefix and payload.\n\nReady responses retain the empty-queue decode bypass. Replay enqueues during instruction-bus stalls. Every accepted fetch writes the free FIFO slot, including a bypass, which leaves the pointers unchanged. A dequeue from a full FIFO makes its slot available the following cycle.\n\nQueue discard uses the registered pending-target flag. It exposes the corrected PC immediately and rebases the read pointer to the write pointer on the next edge. This removes the direct EX redirect path to the queue pointers while giving the corrected external response the same bypass or enqueue behavior. The pending-target flag masks replay and new fill captures. Redirects without predictor training register a global invalidation pulse with priority over stream validity writes.\n\nThe pipeline tests cover the 16-word limit on a predicted fall-through, row collisions and contiguous replacement, a redirect with replayed stores queued, and refetch after a store modifies a learned instruction followed by FENCE.I.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator lint and `make test TARGET=bench` passed.\n- `make cosim TARGET=bench NRET=1` passed selftest and three random ELFs with and without stalls. Stalled CoreMark produced all five canonical CRCs and printed `Correct operation validated.` The explicit `NRET=1` selects the bench core's existing RVFI width.\n- Stalled CoreMark took 3,758,572 marked cycles, down 6.39% from 4,015,275.\n- Gowin placement options 0, 1, and 2 reached 79.030, 79.292, and 79.292 MHz. The 79.292 MHz median yields 210.96 CoreMark iterations/s, up 9.39% from the 77.436 MHz champion at its marked cycle count.\n- The replay storage grew option 0 to 7,539 logic cells and 1,104 registers. EX recovery is on the longest path, with the divider close on options 1 and 2.\n- Local formal was incomplete within the wall-clock budget. The unchanged `formal/run_all.sh` gate reported 14 of 53 checks passing on the selected RTL, including illegal-instruction trapping, order uniqueness, liveness, and both PC checks. Zero failures or counterexamples were reported. Bitwuzla spent substantially longer unrolling the registered queue discard design, and the register consistency check was still solving.\n\n/srv/hwebench/toolchain/oss-cad-suite/bin/btormc\n/srv/hwebench/toolchain/oss-cad-suite/bin/boolector\n/srv/hwebench/toolchain/oss-cad-suite/bin/bitwuzla\n/srv/hwebench/toolchain/oss-cad-suite/bin/z3\nHWE_AGENT_TMP\nGOWIN_HOME\nTMPDIR\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
