{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_151","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 -c 'from pathlib import Path; from xml.etree import ElementTree as x; ps=list(Path(\\\"cores/bench/test\\\").glob(\\\"*.result.xml\\\")); print([(p.name,len(list(x.parse(p).iter(\\\"testcase\\\")))) for p in sorted(ps)]); print(sum(len(list(x.parse(p).iter(\\\"testcase\\\"))) for p in ps))'; sed -n '1,80p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md; git check-ignore -v cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"[('test_alu_runner.result.xml', 9), ('test_decoder_runner.result.xml', 30), ('test_div_unit_runner.result.xml', 6), ('test_if_stage_runner.result.xml', 4), ('test_imm_gen_runner.result.xml', 8), ('test_mul_unit_runner.result.xml', 3), ('test_pipeline_runner.result.xml', 26), ('test_reg_file_runner.result.xml', 5)]\n91\n# Pipelined instruction replay\n\nIF uses a 512-entry direct-mapped replay table. Each packed block RAM row holds a word, the 21 remaining PC tag bits, and a valid bit. An accepted fetch advances the fetch PC and reads the predicted successor on the same edge. A coincident fill overrides the RAM output, including when the replacement tag causes a miss. Ready external words have priority, and either source can bypass an empty FIFO.\n\nThe four-entry FIFO keeps a registered head PC. Dequeue promotes the next buffered address or takes the incoming PC when replacing the last entry. Redirects discard the old queue and require a ready response at the corrected address before replay can resume. EX sees the fetch PC when the queue is empty, even on an instruction-bus stall.\n\nReset and non-training redirects, including FENCE.I, disable replay and clear the packed RAM through the write port over 512 edges. External fetch can continue throughout the scrub. A new invalidation during an active pass can use the rows that pass already cleared. The replay path holds its read and collision state when fetch holds.\n\nDecode readiness is independent of fetch validity, so a late redirect can suppress ID issue without routing through FIFO pointer updates. EX checks the JALR successor with carry-save comparison and still produces the resolved target from the address adder. The divider captures its first quotient digit and remainder and the small-divisor cutoff at launch. The divider keeps the same eight-edge transfer schedule and ALTOPS behavior.\n\nThe tests exercise cold tag misses, replacement and collisions, ready-word priority, replay bypass and enqueue, queue promotion and holds, redirects to already cached addresses, and refetch after an instruction store and FENCE.I.\n\n## Local checks\n\nVerification is in progress.\n.gitignore:87:cores/*/implementation_notes.md\tcores/bench/implementation_notes.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
