{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_52","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 -c 'import json; a=json.loads(open(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\\\").readlines()[-2]); print(a[\\\"hypothesis\\\"][\\\"hypothesis\\\"])'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_52","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 -c 'import json; a=json.loads(open(\\\"cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl\\\").readlines()[-2]); print(a[\\\"hypothesis\\\"][\\\"hypothesis\\\"])'\"","aggregated_output":"Let validated BEQ and BNE enter EX immediately behind their load producer.\nFor a real nonzero register dependency on the aligned EX/MEM load, record\nwhich operands need that load and select the other forwarded operand\nbefore the register so the late lane needs one comparator. Capture the\nsequential and relative target PCs and their matches against the oldest\nunissued address. Hold the branch behind the older bus access through\ndmem backpressure. Register load forwarding eligibility with the producer\nusing its effective address and width. An unaligned producer traps and an\noperand read takes the next older forwarded value or the register value.\nOther load-use interlocks retain their current behavior.\n\nAt the next stage, resolve that branch against the registered MEM/WB load\nvalue, including the normal signed or unsigned subword extraction. For\nBEQ/BNE with both sources equal to the load destination, equality is true.\nFinish its RVFI record with the actual operands and next PC. Preserve\nthe existing taken-misaligned branch trap and suppress training on it.\nWhen the prediction is correct, allow the younger EX slot to proceed.\nOn a late mismatch, annul that slot before any memory or M-unit request.\nRegister the correction candidates and the resolved choice, and discard\nthe wrong-path FIFO when the registered correction takes over fetch.\nHold the corrected address across imem stalls and seed replay from the\naccepted corrected word. Capture the resolving branch's completed result\nin the commit register and release it on the following edge, as the\nregistered redirect takes effect. The annulled younger slot leaves that\ncommit edge free. This preserves the retirement gap to a corrected DIV\nor REM within the existing liveness window. Gate younger side effects\nwith the mismatch bit and keep bulk payload enables driven by registered\nholds. Continue to retire exactly one instruction per valid RVFI event.\n\nCapture the ordinary and late predictor updates separately, then arbitrate\nthe single predictor write port using the registered valid bits. Give a\nwrong-path update no eligibility. Keep the late verdict off the replay\nRAM's write enable. An invalidating redirect must hide replay immediately\nand scrub the arrays before replay can be used again, including any word\nwritten just as the scrub is requested.\n\nA scratch registered-recovery implementation passed the canonical\nCoreMark CRCs in 3,405,608 marked cycles with both stalls enabled, down\n3.80 percent. Its first Gowin option-1 result was 77.564 MHz, short of\nthe required 84.45 MHz median at those cycles. The proposed separate\npending update records, registered commit hold and replay write-enable\nisolation address timing in that prototype. The refined scratch version\nreproduced that cycle count and matched the ISS on selftest and three\nrandom programs with both bus stalls. At 86 MHz and those cycles the\ndesign would deliver 252.52 iterations/sec. Check all placements, the\nCoreMark CRCs and the unchanged single-retire formal liveness gate.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
