{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_5", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/core.yaml && tail -125 cores/bench/LESSONS.md && git check-ignore -v implementation_notes.md cores/bench/implementation_notes.md'", "aggregated_output": "name: bench\ndescription: Frozen LLM-benchmark fixture core. Identical RTL to baseline at the bench-fixture-v1\n  freeze point. The benchmark matrix clones from the bench-fixture-v1 orphan branch\n  and operates only on this directory.\nisa: rv32im\nnret: 1\ntarget_fpga: tang-nano-20k\ntargets:\n  fmax_mhz: 135\n  lut4: 10000\n  coremark_iter_s: 300\n  coremark_per_mhz: 2.2\ncurrent:\n  fmax_mhz: 91.689\n  lut4: 5659\n  ff: 939\n  coremark_iter_s: 3.0e-06\n  coremark_per_mhz: 0.0\n  source_id: hyp-20261120-003-r12s2\n  updated: '2026-11-20T15:40:16.820308Z'\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-001-r1s0 (improvement, +729.95%): Replacing combinational `/` and `%` with a shared, blocking radix-4 divider removed the long EX ALU path and raised median Gowin Fmax from 5.442 to 45.180 MHz, with unchanged CoreMark cycles because no divide or remainder retired between the markers to incur the eight-cycle EX stall.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-003-r1s2 (regression, +8.42%): Avoiding redirects with a 64-entry tagged next-PC table cut stalled CoreMark cycles by 6.04%, with the combinational EX divider still limiting median Gowin Fmax to 5.546 MHz and leaving throughput well behind the round winner, whose clocked divider raised Fmax to 45.180 MHz.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-001-r2s0 (regression, +5.23%): Driving fetch directly from the registered EX/MEM redirect target while invalidating the younger EX slot preserved CoreMark's cycle count and removed the EX-to-IF-to-ID redirect path from Gowin's worst paths, leaving the register-file-to-data-memory path through the EX ALU to cap median Fmax at 47.542 MHz.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-002-r2s1 (regression, +13.90%): A one-entry fall-through fetch buffer cut stalled CoreMark cycles by 3.07% by saving ready instructions during load-use and backend holds for later instruction-bus stalls, and using the registered full bit to select the decode payload while applying redirects to ID/EX validity removed the wide redirect path from Gowin's worst-path reports as median Fmax rose from 45.180 to 49.878 MHz.\n- 2026-11-20 h\n…[11027 of 14099 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:a7f61da897bff3be]…\n terms to the one-hot operand forwarding muxes, and the full routed path through forwarding and the ALU carry chain grew from 16.201 to 16.444 ns on Gowin, cutting CoreMark throughput at unchanged cycle count.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-002-r13s1 (regression, +0.41%): Forwarding the registered low-half MUL product from MEM/WB into MEM let adjacent dependent ADDs and stores dependent only on write data issue without bubbles, cutting stalled CoreMark cycles by 2.69%, with fetch replay and its issue feedback capping median Gowin Fmax at 89.587 MHz against the 93.329 MHz needed for acceptance.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-003-r13s2 (regression, -2.07%): Bypassing the load-use interlock for BEQ/BNE with registered rollback cut stalled CoreMark cycles by 3.78%, with replay-to-FIFO issue feedback and nearly tied EX forwarding paths into the ALU and divider capping median Gowin Fmax at 86.390 MHz against the 88.22 MHz needed to break even.\n.gitignore:87:cores/*/implementation_notes.md\tcores/bench/implementation_notes.md\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,240p' formal/run_all.sh && sed -n '1,150p' formal/checks_si.cfg && rg -n \\\"\"'^(timing|cosim|fpga|test|formal)|GOWIN|TMPDIR\" Makefile tools/eval/gowin.py'", "aggregated_output": "#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Run riscv-formal checks against the current $RTL_DIR/*.sv.\n# Requires: formal/riscv-formal cloned (manual clone or `git submodule init`).\n#\n# Stages every $RTL_DIR/*.sv plus wrapper.sv + the chosen checks config under\n# the riscv-formal tree, then runs sby -> bitwuzla via the framework's\n# generated makefile. Tallies PASS/FAIL by inspecting each task's\n# logfile.txt.\n#\n# Usage: bash formal/run_all.sh [checks-cfg-path]\n#   default: formal/checks.cfg       (fast, ALTOPS, used by orchestrator)\n#   deep   : formal/checks-deep.cfg  (no ALTOPS, proves M-ext arithmetic)\n#\n# Env vars (orchestrator-driven, override $1 and defaults):\n#   WRAPPER     — path to wrapper SV (default formal/wrapper.sv)\n#   CHECKS_CFG  — path to checks config (default formal/checks.cfg)\n# When BOTH are unset, the script auto-detects nret from\n# cores/$CORE_NAME/core.yaml: nret=1 routes to wrapper_si.sv +\n# checks_si.cfg; nret=2 (or absent) uses the defaults. Agents\n# invoking `bash formal/run_all.sh` directly therefore get the\n# right wrapper without needing to know the env-var plumbing.\nset -e\n\nif [ -z \"${RTL_DIR:-}\" ] || [ -z \"${CORE_NAME:-}\" ]; then\n  echo \"ERROR: formal/run_all.sh requires RTL_DIR and CORE_NAME env vars.\" >&2\n  echo \"  Example: RTL_DIR=cores/v1/rtl CORE_NAME=v1 bash formal/run_all.sh formal/checks.cfg\" >&2\n  exit 2\nfi\n\nSCRIPT_DIR=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\" && pwd)\"\nPROJECT_ROOT=\"$(cd \"$SCRIPT_DIR/..\" && pwd)\"\nRISCV_FORMAL=\"$SCRIPT_DIR/riscv-formal\"\n# Per-invocation work dir + log, unique among every process sharing this\n# riscv-formal checkout (the K concurrent agents of a run share it through\n# their worktrees'