{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_147","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 -c 'from pathlib import Path; import xml.etree.ElementTree as X; cases=[case for p in Path(\\\"cores/bench/test\\\").glob(\\\"*.result.xml\\\") for case in X.parse(p).iter(\\\"testcase\\\")]; print(len(cases), \\\"cases\\\", sum(case.find(\\\"failure\\\") is not None for case in cases), \\\"failed\\\")' && nl -ba implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":"88 cases 0 failed\n     1\t# Instruction replay lookahead\n     2\t\n     3\tFetch launches a synchronous 1,024-word payload RAM read when it accepts a word. The registered payload follows the tagged BTB successor or the sequential PC. An asynchronous descriptor lookup checks the current full tag and the requested word's bit in one of 128 eight-word sectors.\n     4\t\n     5\tThe ready bus response takes priority. A replay hit can issue directly through an empty FIFO or enter a slot that was free at cycle start. EX sees the oldest unissued full PC throughout a hold. The first corrected request waits for the external response and uses its successor to restart lookahead.\n     6\t\n     7\tOnly accepted external misses stage a fill. A pending fill supplies the newest tag and mask for its sector. A replacement starts a new mask, and the descriptor and payload commit together. A registered write index detects a collision with the held read after the RAM edge and blocks that read until fetch advances. Reset and the registered non-training redirect pulse invalidate every sector and suppress replay and fills during invalidation.\n     8\t\n     9\tThe directed pipeline tests cover 20 stalled fall-through words with contiguous retirement, aliased sectors at `0x40` and `0x1040`, and a same-word read/write collision held across three stalled cycles. The FENCE.I, wrong-path side-effect, and retirement checks remain in the suite.\n    10\t\n    11\tThe initial replay implementation reproduced the expected cycle count, but the divider's first byte limited the median clock. The final build captures two divisor magnitude predicates when the divider accepts operands. This moves the width checks ahead of the first prefix step and preserves the calculation and latency. The divider test exercises signed operands around both cutoffs.\n    12\t\n    13\t## Local verification\n    14\t\n    15\t- Yosys proved fetch equivalence to the champion with `imem_ready` high and proved that the new divider predicates equal the original magnitude tests for every 32-bit divisor in both signedness modes.\n    16\t- Gowin placement options 0, 1, and 2 reached 76.388, 78.390, and 78.390 MHz. Option 0 used 5,917 logic cells, 1,183 registers, and six block RAMs. The median and 3,528,765 marked cycles yield 222.15 iterations/s, 5.30% above the champion's 210.96 iterations/s.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
