{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path('.tmp/agent-logs/impl.hyp-20261120-001-r15s0.log')\nfor line in p.open():\n    try:\n        entry = json.loads(line)\n    except ValueError:\n        continue\n    item = entry.get('item', {})\n    if entry.get('type') == 'item.completed' and item.get('type') == 'agent_message':\n        print(item.get('text', ''))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"I’ll inspect the bench pipeline and verification targets, then implement the load-response paths and run the local gates.\nThe first RTL version passes lint and single-retirement co-simulation, including the stalled CoreMark CRC check. Formal and all three Gowin placements are running. I’m adding directed checks for carry, trap fallback, and recovery while both buses stall.\nCoreMark completed in 3,294,730 marked cycles, matching the cycle target. The first two routed versions fell short of 90.56 MHz, with ordinary EX forwarding and branch recovery among the longest paths. I’m routing the changes that shorten those paths.\nThe directed checks pass for carry into the upper word, 32-bit wraparound, trapped-producer fallback, and recovery under concurrent bus stalls. All three placements completed for the strongest measured version so far, at an 85.319 MHz median. I’m checking the remaining routes and the formal results before selecting the final RTL.\nImplemented exact load-response forwarding in `cores/bench`. Stalled CoreMark matched the **3,294,730-cycle** target. Verilator lint, all eight cocotb runners, and co-simulation passed.\n\nAll three Gowin placements routed. The **86.822 MHz** median fell below the 90.56 MHz promotion threshold. Formal ended with **34 of 53 checks passed**, including bounded liveness, with no counterexamples reported. [Implementation notes](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-sol_xhigh-v2-rep2/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261120-001-r15s0/cores/bench/implementation_notes.md)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
