e annulling the younger EX slot as the target enters ID/EX keeps misses to one bubble, letting the tagged successor predictor cut stalled CoreMark cycles by 6.04% as median Gowin Fmax rises from 45.180 to 49.767 MHz.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-001-r3s0 (regression, +9.88%): Registering the shared DSP product in EX/MEM exposed the divider’s three cascaded rad\n…[4524 of 7596 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:4d0fd1ad00a0ea6a]…\n0261120-002-r7s1 (regression, +8.32%): Choosing the prefix length by divisor magnitude and using parallel trial subtracts for one radix-32 or radix-8 digit per edge preserved the eight-edge transfer schedule and shifted Gowin's timing limit to EX result and recovery paths, raising median Fmax from 77.436 to 83.877 MHz at unchanged CoreMark cycles for 455 extra logic cells.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-003-r7s2 (improvement, +9.39%): Replaying learned BTB successor words during instruction-bus stalls cut CoreMark cycles by 6.39%, and writing every accepted word into a FIFO slot free at cycle start, even on decode bypass, removed decode acceptance from the RAM write enable and helped reach 79.292 MHz median Gowin Fmax.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-001-r8s0 (regression, +0.46%): Sharing the low bits of the odd divisor multiples through 7D and narrowing the radix-16/radix-8 trial subtracts saved 171 logic cells on Gowin option 0, while EX recovery limited Fmax in all three placements at unchanged CoreMark cycle count.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
