{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '96,148p' tools/tournament.py\nls -la .tmp/agent-logs\"","aggregated_output":"def pick_winner(entries: list[dict],\n                current_best: float,\n                current_lut: float | None = None,\n                coremark_target: float | None = None,\n                lut_target: float | None = None) -> Optional[dict]:\n    \"\"\"Return the round's winner via the accept-rule module.\n\n    With no targets set, behavior is identical to the legacy \"highest\n    fitness > current_best\" rule. With targets set, accept() is called\n    per-candidate with (perf, lut) tuples.\n\n    Tie-break: among candidates that all pass accept, prefer the one\n    that maximizes (fitness, -lut4, -slot). This degenerates to the\n    legacy \"highest fitness, lowest slot\" tie-break when LUT is\n    unconstrained.\n    \"\"\"\n    from tools.accept_rule import accept\n\n    valid = [e for e in entries\n             if isinstance(e.get(\"fitness\"), (int, float))]\n    if not valid:\n        return None\n\n    old = (current_best, current_lut)\n\n    candidates = []\n    for e in valid:\n        new = (e[\"fitness\"], e.get(\"lut4\"))\n        if accept(old, new,\n                  coremark_target=coremark_target, lut_target=lut_target):\n            candidates.append(e)\n\n    if not candidates:\n        return None\n    # A missing LUT4 ranks worst, never best (0 would win the tie-break).\n    def _lut(e):\n        v = e.get(\"lut4\")\n        return v if isinstance(v, (int, float)) else float(\"inf\")\n    return max(candidates,\n               key=lambda e: (e[\"fitness\"], -_lut(e), -e[\"slot\"]))\n\n\n# Per-phase capacity, per orchestrator process. Both gates are CPU gates:\n#\n# - formal=1: run_all.sh runs `make -j<ncpu>` over ~50-100 SBY tasks. Each\n#   invocation stages into its own formal/riscv-formal/cores/<core>-<pid>/\n#   dir, so concurrent runs no longer corrupt each other, but two at once\n#   halve each one's CPU and push slow SMT problems past the 45-minute\n#   timeout (recorded as broken). Across processes (bench --parallel reps,\n#   two `make loop`s) the same contention is prevented by the machine-wide\n#   lock in phase_gate below.\n#\n# - fpga=1: each slot's run_fpga_eval already forks 3 parallel nextpnr\ntotal 1124\ndrwxrwx---+ 2 nobody nogroup   4096 Nov 20 03:54 .\ndrwxrwx--T+ 5 nobody nogroup   4096 Nov 20 03:52 ..\n-rw-rw----+ 1 nobody nogroup 302299 Nov 20 03:48 impl.hyp-20261120-001-r1s0.log\n-rw-rw----+ 1 nobody nogroup 438817 Nov 20 03:47 impl.hyp-20261120-002-r1s1.log\n-rw-rw----+ 1 nobody nogroup 211720 Nov 20 03:51 impl.hyp-20261120-003-r1s2.log\n-rw-rw----+ 1 nobody nogroup    454 Nov 20 03:35 scribe.baseline-bench-74169ac.log\n-rw-rw----+ 1 nobody nogroup   4787 Nov 20 03:53 scribe.hyp-20261120-001-r1s0.log\n-rw-rw----+ 1 nobody nogroup 163246 Nov 20 03:54 scribe.hyp-20261120-002-r1s1.log\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
