{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg 'hyp-20261120-00[123]-r9s' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python -c 'import json,sys; keys=(\\\"id\\\",\\\"motivation\\\",\\\"hypothesis\\\",\\\"changes\\\"); [print(*(r.get(k) for k in keys),sep=\\\"\\\\n\\\",end=\\\"\\\\n\\\\n\\\") for r in map(json.loads,sys.stdin)]'; git log -12 --oneline\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261120-001-r9s0\nThe champion retired 135,320 BEQ/BNE instructions that immediately\nconsumed a load in the 3,540,112-cycle CoreMark interval. A scratch\ncombinational bypass passed the canonical CRCs in 3,406,310 cycles,\nbut reached only 58.434 MHz in Gowin placement option 1 because the\ndata memory path extended through EX into fetch recovery. Resolving\nthis branch in MEM can use the already registered load result while\neliminating the issue bubble.\n\n{'motivation': 'The champion retired 135,320 BEQ/BNE instructions that immediately\\nconsumed a load in the 3,540,112-cycle CoreMark interval. A scratch\\ncombinational bypass passed the canonical CRCs in 3,406,310 cycles,\\nbut reached only 58.434 MHz in Gowin placement option 1 because the\\ndata memory path extended through EX into fetch recovery. Resolving\\nthis branch in MEM can use the already registered load result while\\neliminating the issue bubble.\\n', 'hypothesis': \"Exempt aligned BEQ/BNE encodings from the adjacent load-use bubble.\\nUse the existing EX/MEM producer tag match to recognize the dependency\\nin EX. Qualify the producer's register-write eligibility before\\nlatching EX/MEM by checking alignment with the low two bits of the\\neffective address. This keeps the alignment check out of the ordinary\\nEX forwarding mux and lets a branch behind a trapping load use the\\nolder valid value. An unready load still holds EX through the existing\\ndmem stall. Retain the load-use interlock for other consumers.\\n\\nFor the bypassed branch, register its dependency 