{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_32","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg --files cores/bench/test; cat formal/checks_si.cfg; rg -n -A6 '\"'^test:|''^timing:'\"' Makefile; git ls-files cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses\"","aggregated_output":"cores/bench/test/test_imm_gen.py\ncores/bench/test/conftest.py\ncores/bench/test/test_div_unit.py\ncores/bench/test/test_if_stage.py\ncores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\ncores/bench/test/_helpers.py\ncores/bench/test/test_decoder.py\ncores/bench/test/test_reg_file.py\ncores/bench/test/test_mul_unit.py\ncores/bench/test/test_alu.py\n[options]\nisa rv32im\nnret 1\nsolver bitwuzla\n\n[depth]\n# BMC depth per check. 2nd column (where present) is the k-induction prove\n# depth. Keep depths matched to the current pipeline so bugs within ~20\n# cycles of any symbolic instruction stream are exposed.\ninsn          20\nreg       10  20\npc_fwd    10  20\npc_bwd    10  20\ncausal    10  20\n# unique   — no two retirements share rvfi_order (catches double-retire)\n# cover    — sanity that the CPU retires (prevents vacuous-pass suites)\n# ill      — illegal instructions must trap; rvfi_trap from decoder.is_illegal\n# liveness — CPU makes forward progress under any symbolic stream\nunique     1 10 20\ncover      1    20\nill             20\nliveness   1 10 20\n\n[defines]\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALIGNED_MEM\n# RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS — fast mode. Same as checks.cfg. See checks.cfg for\n# the full rationale on what ALTOPS does and does not prove. M-extension\n# arithmetic correctness is covered by test/test_alu.py and `make formal-deep`.\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\n\n[cover]\n# Sanity cover: the CPU must retire at least one non-trapping instruction.\nalways @* if (!reset) cover (rvfi_valid && !rvfi_trap);\n\n[verilog-files]\n# run_all.sh rebuilds this section from the actual rtl/ glob; the list\n# below is overwritten before genchecks runs. Kept as a placeholder so\n# the section is syntactically present for any reader inspecting the cfg.\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/core.sv\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/wrapper.sv\n106:test:\n107-\tpytest -v $(TEST_DIR)/\n108-\n109-test-infra:\n110-\tpytest -v tools/\n111-\n112-cosim: cosim-build bench/programs/selftest.elf bench/programs/coremark.elf\n--\n140:timing:\n141-\tpython3 -m tools.eval.gowin $(TARGET)\n142-\n143-bench/programs/coremark.elf: bench/programs/Makefile bench/programs/crt0.S \\\n144-                              $(wildcard bench/programs/coremark/*.c) \\\n145-                              $(wildcard bench/programs/coremark/*.h) \\\n146-                              $(wildcard bench/programs/coremark/baremetal/*.c) \\\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
