the next replay entry on that edge. Hold\\nthe RAM output and its collision metadata when fetch holds. The ready\\nexternal response and registered replay result become two producers of\\nthe existing fall-through FIFO. A ready response has priority. When\\nthe external bus stalls, a valid, exact-tag replay hit can bypass an\\nempty FIFO directly into ID or enqueue if decode is blocked. Preserve\\nFIFO order and the existing BTB prediction and recovery policy.\\n\\nRegister the FIFO head PC separately from its instruction payload \n…[20973 of 24045 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:fcb54833bb5480a5]…\nefore the final two predictor cases were added. The expanded suite passed on a later timing trial, and its rerun on the selected RTL was still in progress at handoff.\\n- Stalled CoreMark completed ten iterations in 3,402,673 marked cycles. The canonical CRCs and validation message matched, and the simulator reported no out-of-bounds accesses.\\n- Gowin placement options 0, 1, and 2 reached 82.478, 79.703, and 79.703 MHz. The 79.703 MHz median gives 234.24 iterations per second and falls short of the approximately 84.38 MHz acceptance threshold for this cycle count. Option 0 used 5,774 logic cells, 1,245 registers, and six block RAMs. The median placement's critical path crosses EX branch resolution into fetch replay invalidation.\\n- Local formal is incomplete. The initial liveness failure is described above. The recovery fix passed liveness on subsequent variants. The full run on the selected RTL remained in progress at handoff.\\n\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-20T12:40:04.047778Z\",\n  \"slot\": 2,\n  \"round_id\": 10\n}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
