{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_3", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'find .. -maxdepth 3 -name AGENTS.md -print && cat schemas/hypothesis.schema.json && cat cores/bench/LESSONS.md'", "aggregated_output": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"required\": [\"id\",\"title\",\"category\",\"motivation\",\"hypothesis\",\"expected_impact\",\"changes\"],\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"id\":       {\"type\": \"string\", \"pattern\": \"^hyp-[0-9]{8}-[0-9]{3}(-r[0-9]+s[0-9]+)?$\"},\n    \"title\":    {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 5},\n    \"category\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"micro_opt\",\"structural\",\"extension\",\"predictor\",\"memory\"]},\n    \"motivation\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"hypothesis\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"required\": [\"fitness_delta_pct\",\"confidence\"],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"fitness_delta_pct\": {\"type\": \"integer\"},\n        \"confidence\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"low\",\"medium\",\"high\"]}\n      }\n    },\n    \"changes\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\", \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\"file\",\"description\"],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"file\":        {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Must be under rtl/ (any extension) or be a test/test_*.py cocotb suite. Anything else is rejected by the runtime sandbox check.\",\n            \"pattern\": \"^(rtl/[^.].*|test/test_[^/]+\\\\.py)$\"\n          },\n          \"description\": {\"type\": \"string\"}\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-001-r1s0 (improvement, +729.95%): Replacing combinational `/` and `%` with a shared, blocking radix-4 divider removed the long EX ALU path and raised median Gowin Fmax from 5.442 to 45.180 MHz, with unchanged CoreMark cycles because no divide or remainder retired between the markers to incur the eight-cycle EX stall.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-003-r1s2 (regression, +8.42%): Avoiding redirects with a 64-entry tagged next-PC table cut stalled CoreMark cycles by 6.04%, with the combinational EX divider still limiting median Gowin Fmax to 5.546 MHz and leaving throughput well behind the round winner, whose clocked divider raised Fmax to 45.180 MHz.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120\n…[10699 of 13771 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:a7841ffda4f21bd0]…\nadvance while the load-use interlock held immediate consumers for MEM/WB forwarding, cutting stalled CoreMark cycles by 1.67% with the divider's prefix trial logic capping median Gowin Fmax at 89.170 MHz, below the 89.589 MHz needed for acceptance.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-002-r12s1 (regression, +1.31%): Moving the load-use interlock into ID/EX removed replayed source fields from fetch FIFO pop and head promotion at unchanged stalled CoreMark cycles, with paths from the registered MEM/WB match to the ALU subtract result and from the EX/MEM result to the divider prefix capping median Gowin Fmax at 88.248 MHz, below the 91.11 MHz acceptance threshold.\n- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-003-r12s2 (improvement, +5.26%): Training a source/target `PC[10:2]` match bit lets IF skip same-row replay BRAM fills while accepting ready bus words, removing last-fill forwarding and raising Fmax at unchanged stalled CoreMark cycle count when paired with direction selection after registering the EX target and fall-through rejections.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
