{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg 'hyp-20261120-(00[123]-r12s[012]|001-r6s0|001-r7s0)' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import json,sys; fields=(\\\"id\\\",\\\"fitness\\\",\\\"fmax_mhz\\\",\\\"cycles\\\",\\\"lut4\\\",\\\"seeds\\\",\\\"perturbations\\\",\\\"critical_path\\\",\\\"logic_levels\\\",\\\"implementation_notes\\\"); rows=[json.loads(l) for l in sys.stdin]; print(*[{k:r.get(k) for k in fields} for r in rows],sep=\\\"\\\\n\\\\n\\\")'\"", "aggregated_output": "{'id': 'hyp-20261120-001-r6s0', 'fitness': 178.3, 'fmax_mhz': 76.909, 'cycles': 4313521, 'lut4': 4928, 'seeds': [73.993, 76.909, 76.909], 'perturbations': [[0, 73.993, 11], [1, 76.909, 15], [2, 76.909, 15]], 'critical_path': {'from': 'cpu/u_id/reg_q.fwd_rs1_sel_1_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_if/recovery_pc_q_19_s0', 'slack_ns': -8.515, 'arrival_ns': 18.809, 'logic_cells': 27, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_if', 'cpu/u_ex']}, 'logic_levels': 11, 'implementation_notes': \"# Register arithmetic and forwarding selects before use\\n\\nID compares both raw source tags against the nonzero destinations in EX and MEM. The existing forwarding priority logic qualifies those matches with each producer's next write eligibility and registers the resulting masks in ID/EX. EX checks link alignment using the JAL immediate or the forwarded JALR sum. MEM uses the same misalignment check for forwarding eligibility and writeback. The existing dmem hold retains both the masks and producer values while MEM/WB clears retirement valid. The M units and RVFI operand registers capture the forwarded operands at the request handshake.\\n\\nID also registers the 11 RV32I operation enables. EX combines the masked integer datapath, link, multiply, and divide results with an OR. The standalone encoded ALU wraps the same integer datapath. The divider captures both prefix cutoff flags directly from the request divisor and signedness. The negative cutoff excludes exact magnitudes 16 and 256 by testing for a nonzero low slice.\\n\\nThe divider keeps the existing prefix mux structure. A trial that folded the byte cutoff into each quotient digit mask reduced median Fmax to 73.319 MHz, so the implementation retains the registered cutoff as the mux select.\\n\\nThe directed tests cover misaligned JAL, JALR, and load producers with older writes to the same register. Divider coverage includes signed quotient and remainder on both sides of the negative cutoffs, and changes the divisor input after launch to check capture.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- Verilator lint pas\n…[10554 of 13626 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:4b8ff0398f971ebb]…\nandom programs also passed with instruction and data stalls.\\n- Stalled CoreMark passed the canonical CRCs and completed 10 iterations in\\n  3,489,128 marked cycles.\\n- Gowin placement options 0, 1, and 2 reached 85.003, 88.248, and\\n  88.248 MHz. The median gives 252.92 CoreMark iterations per second and\\n  falls below the 91.11 MHz acceptance threshold at this cycle count.\\n  The longest median paths run from the registered MEM/WB match into the\\n  ALU subtract result and from the EX/MEM result into the divider prefix.\\n\"}\n\n{'id': 'hyp-20261120-003-r12s2', 'fitness': 262.78, 'fmax_mhz': 91.689, 'cycles': 3489128, 'lut4': 5659, 'seeds': [88.627, 91.689, 91.689], 'perturbations': [[0, 88.627, 13], [1, 91.689, 14], [2, 91.689, 14]], 'critical_path': {'from': 'cpu/u_mem/reg_q.write_result_0_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_0_s0', 'slack_ns': -6.283, 'arrival_ns': 16.577, 'logic_cells': 13, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}, 'logic_levels': 13, 'implementation_notes': ''}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
