{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg -n -i 'shifter|barrel|carry.select|carry.lookahead|split.*add|segmented|borrow' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import json,sys,re; p=re.compile(r\\\"shifter|barrel|carry.select|carry.lookahead|split.*add|segmented|borrow\\\",re.I); [print((r[\\\"id\\\"],r[\\\"category\\\"],[(m.start(),s) for s in r.get(\\\"implementation_notes\\\",\\\"\\\").splitlines() if (m:=p.search(s))][:5])) for line in sys.stdin if (r:=json.loads(line.split(\\\":\\\",1)[1]))]'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg -n -i 'shifter|barrel|carry.select|carry.lookahead|split.*add|segmented|borrow' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import json,sys,re; p=re.compile(r\\\"shifter|barrel|carry.select|carry.lookahead|split.*add|segmented|borrow\\\",re.I); [print((r[\\\"id\\\"],r[\\\"category\\\"],[(m.start(),s) for s in r.get(\\\"implementation_notes\\\",\\\"\\\").splitlines() if (m:=p.search(s))][:5])) for line in sys.stdin if (r:=json.loads(line.split(\\\":\\\",1)[1]))]'\"","aggregated_output":"('hyp-20261120-001-r1s0', 'micro_opt', [])\n('hyp-20261120-002-r1s1', 'structural', [])\n('hyp-20261120-002-r3s1', 'structural', [])\n('hyp-20261120-001-r4s0', 'micro_opt', [])\n('hyp-20261120-002-r4s1', 'structural', [])\n('hyp-20261120-001-r5s0', 'micro_opt', [(339, '- The divider consumes the first byte with a four-bit table lookup and parallel 13-bit differences. Constant products provide the narrow divisor multiples. The same work edge registers wide odd multiples, with even multiples derived by shifts. The next six edges each consume a nibble with fifteen parallel 37-bit differences and adjacent borrow flags. The held quotient or remainder is sign-corrected for transfer eight edges after capture. ALTOPS retains its registered result timing and formulas.')])\n('hyp-20261120-002-r5s1', 'structural', [(113, \"- A parameterized digit circuit implements the radix-4 and radix-8 steps with parallel subtractions and adjacent borrow flags. The shared register's mutually exclusive input selects are implemented with masks to keep selection parallel.\")])\n('hyp-20261120-002-r7s1', 'structural', [(107, \"Six work edges consume five bits per narrow digit or three per wide digit. Parallel subtracts and adjacent borrow flags select the digit and residual. The narrow residual fits in 14 bits. The wide trial fits in 32 bits, and each wide candidate also checks the upper bits of its 35-bit multiple. The lanes have separate residual registers and share a dividend and quotient shift register with one-hot inputs for capture, setup, and each lane's digit step.\"), (255, \"- `make fpga TARGET=bench` reported 75.973, 83.877, and 83.877 MHz using 5,504 logic cells. The median gives 208.89 CoreMark iterations per second, up 8.3% from 192.85. EX result and recovery paths limit timing. The placement spread is 7.904 MHz, and the split adds 455 logic cells to the champion's 5,049.\")])\n('hyp-20261120-001-r8s0', 'micro_opt', [(333, '- The narrow lane finishes the byte prefix on the setup edge, then consumes six four-bit digits with 17-bit trial subtracts and a 12-bit residual. The wide lane uses three 17-bit prefix trials over the top 14 dividend bits, then consumes six three-bit digits. Its seven work trials reject 35-bit multiples with an upper bit set or a borrow from the low 32 bits.')])\n('hyp-20261120-001-r11s0', 'micro_opt', [])\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
