{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg -n -i 'launch|result_latency|edges|cycle' cores/bench/test/test_alu.py | tail -35 && rg -n 'CoreMark|rem|div' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import json,sys; r=[json.loads(l.split(\\\":\\\",1)[1]) for l in sys.stdin]; print([row[\\\"implementation_notes\\\"][:2800] for row in r if row[\\\"id\\\"] in {\\\"hyp-20261120-001-r1s0\\\",\\\"hyp-20261120-001-r9s0\\\"}])'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_29", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n -i 'launch|result_latency|edges|cycle' cores/bench/test/test_alu.py | tail -35 && rg -n 'CoreMark|rem|div' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import json,sys; r=[json.loads(l.split(\\\":\\\",1)[1]) for l in sys.stdin]; print([row[\\\"implementation_notes\\\"][:2800] for row in r if row[\\\"id\\\"] in {\\\"hyp-20261120-001-r1s0\\\",\\\"hyp-20261120-001-r9s0\\\"}])'\"", "aggregated_output": "[\"# Shared radix-4 divider in EX\\n\\nDIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU now share a blocking divider. It captures forwarded operands when the older EX/MEM instruction can advance. Six clocks consume the 36-bit padded dividend at three radix-4 digits per clock, and the seventh registers the sign-corrected result. EX/MEM accepts the result eight cycles after capture when ready. During the wait, ID/EX and fetch hold while older instructions drain and EX/MEM receives bubbles with writeback and memory enables cleared. The result returns through the usual EX/MEM forwarding path. ALTOPS captures the original substitute value at request time and uses the same handshake and latency.\\n\\nThe divider reuses the dividend shift register to accumulate quotient digits and derives 2D by shifting the registered D. The radix-4 recurrence yields the required divide-by-zero values with quotient negation suppressed. The signed overflow case falls out of the normal 32-bit result selection. Divider vectors moved to a dedicated cocotb runner. The pipeline regression checks that a divide captures a load result across a stalled older store and forwards its quotient immediately to the next instruction.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- Verilator `-Wall` lint passed for both the hardware and ALTOPS builds. The guarded include in `core.sv` supports the requested lint glob, which can list `core.sv` before the compilation-unit types.\\n- All six cocotb runners passed. Divider coverage includes signed and unsigned corner cases, varied operand widths, consecutive requests, and deferred result acceptance.\\n- `bash formal/run_all.sh` passed all 53 single-retirement ALTOPS checks, including liveness, with zero failures and zero fixes. The arithmetic datapath was exercised by cocotb and cosim. The separate `formal-deep` suite was outside this local check.\\n- `make cosim TARGET=bench NRET=1` passed selftest and three random traces with and without stalls, plus the canonical stalled CoreMark CRC check. The run reached EBREAK and reported no out-of-bounds accesses.\\n\\n## Mea\n…[1811 of 4883 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:48c96dcad5bccb8e]…\ne when a late miss targeted a divide. The branch now completes retirement while IF presents the registered recovery address. The corrected path issues on the same edge as before, and the divider keeps its existing schedule. Directed tests cover this sequence, predictor arbitration, held subword loads, both branch polarities, both sources matching, trapping loads, and wrong-path stores and RV32M requests.\\n\\n## Local validation\\n\\n- Verilator lint passed.\\n- All eight cocotb suites and all five co-simulation ELFs passed. Canonical stalled CoreMark passed in 3,402,673 marked cycles for ten iterations, 3.88% fewer cycles than the champion.\\n- The final formal run has passed 52 of 53 checks, including BEQ, BNE, liveness, and both PC consistency checks. The register proof is still running. No counterexample has been reported for this revision.\\n- The measured cycle count requires about 84.38 MHz median Fmax to clear the acceptance margin. Gowin option 0 routed at 80.009 MHz. Options 1 and 2 are still running.\\n\"]\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
