{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_19", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor line in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n r=json.loads(line)\n if r['round_id'] in (7,8) and 'divid' in (r['title']+' '+r['motivation']).lower():\n  print(r['id'],r['title'],r['fmax_mhz'])\n  print(r['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\n  print(r['implementation_notes'][:3300])\nPY\ncat formal/checks_si.cfg\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261120-001-r7s0 Register arithmetic selects and the first divider digit at launch 81.844\nShorten the arithmetic feedback paths without adding a pipeline edge.\nRegister the final one-hot forwarding and ALU operand masks in ID/EX.\nQualify producer tags with the write eligibility of the values about\nto enter EX/MEM and MEM/WB. Use the live EX slot's write intent and\nlink alignment, and MEM's write intent after load alignment. Give\nEX/MEM priority and retain the masks with a held consumer. Keep raw\nregister operand masks for branches, stores, M requests and RVFI.\nRegister one-hot integer result enables and OR the enabled integer\nterms directly with the link and M results.\n\nReuse JALR alignment from the forwarded address sum and JAL alignment\nfrom immediate bit 1. Use the existing full-width successor comparison\nand redirect timing.\n\nIn the divider, begin first-nibble work at request capture. Derive the\ntop four dividend magnitude bits from the raw operand, signedness and\na lower-28-bits-zero check. Derive the low four divisor magnitude bits\nand cutoff in parallel. Register the first-nibble quotient and remainder\nso the first work edge starts directly with the second-nibble trial.\nCapture the byte cutoff at launch too. For a negative divisor, each\ncutoff uses all ones above its low slice and a nonzero low slice. This\nexcludes exact negative magnitudes 16 and 256 at their respective\ncutoffs. Preserve RV32M zero-divisor and signed-overflow results,\nALTOPS formulas, and the eight-edge handshake.\n\nThe scratch RTL placed at 82.493, 87.108 and 87.108 MHz in Gowin and\nused 5,229 logic cells. Stalled CoreMark passed the canonical CRCs in\n4,015,275 marked cycles, giving 216.94 iter/s at the median, 12.49%\nabove the champion. The median placement is limited by registered\nforwarding into IF recovery. All 89 scratch cocotb cases passed.\nSelftest and three random programs matched the ISS with and without\nboth bus stalls. SAT proved the divider launch expressions equivalent\nto their full-width references. The stock single-ret\n…[13847 of 16919 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:f6caaa0da638c5bf]…\nr    — sanity that the CPU retires (prevents vacuous-pass suites)\n# ill      — illegal instructions must trap; rvfi_trap from decoder.is_illegal\n# liveness — CPU makes forward progress under any symbolic stream\nunique     1 10 20\ncover      1    20\nill             20\nliveness   1 10 20\n\n[defines]\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALIGNED_MEM\n# RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS — fast mode. Same as checks.cfg. See checks.cfg for\n# the full rationale on what ALTOPS does and does not prove. M-extension\n# arithmetic correctness is covered by test/test_alu.py and `make formal-deep`.\n`define RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS\n\n[cover]\n# Sanity cover: the CPU must retire at least one non-trapping instruction.\nalways @* if (!reset) cover (rvfi_valid && !rvfi_trap);\n\n[verilog-files]\n# run_all.sh rebuilds this section from the actual rtl/ glob; the list\n# below is overwritten before genchecks runs. Kept as a placeholder so\n# the section is syntactically present for any reader inspecting the cfg.\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/core.sv\n@basedir@/cores/@core@/wrapper.sv\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_20", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'scratch=/srv/hwebench/tmp/4876824c/54bbf982/bench-r14s0.sMKIohRl\ncat > \"$scratch/fast_ex.py\" <<'\"'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport shutil\nimport sys\n\nscratch = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nname, *opts = sys.argv[1:]\nrtl = scratch / name / 'rtl'\nshutil.copytree('cores/bench/rtl', rtl)\nex = rtl / 'ex_stage.sv'\ns = ex.read_text()\nif 'gate' in opts:\n    s = s.replace('  logic        ex_advance, side_effects;', '''  logic        ex_advance, side_effects;\n  logic        legal_advance, link_aligned;''')\n    s = s.replace('  assign side_effects     = ex_advance && \"'!in.ctrl.is_illegal && !misalign_fault;'\"', '''  assign legal_advance   = ex_advance && \"'!in.ctrl.is_illegal;\n  assign side_effects    = legal_advance && !misalign_fault;\n  assign link_aligned    = !in.ctrl.is_jump ||\n                           (in.ctrl.is_jalr ? jalr_aligned : relative_aligned);'\"''')\n    s = s.replace('in.ctrl.reg_write && side_effects', 'in.ctrl.reg_write && legal_advance && link_aligned')\n    s = s.replace('in.ctrl.mem_read  && side_effects', 'in.ctrl.mem_read  && legal_advance')\n    s = s.replace('in.ctrl.mem_write && side_effects', 'in.ctrl.mem_write && legal_advance')\nif 'merge' in opts:\n    ops = [\n        ('ADD', 'a + b'), ('SUB', 'a - b'), ('AND', 'a & b'), ('OR', 'a | b'),\n        ('XOR', 'a \"'^ b'\"'), ('SLT', \\\"{31'b0, \"'$signed(a) < $signed(b)}\"),\n        ('\"'SLTU', \\\"{31'b0, a < b}\\\"), ('SLL', 'a << b[4:0]'),\n        ('SRL', 'a >> b[4:0]'), ('SRA', '\"'$unsigned($signed(a) >>> b[4:0])'\"'),\n        ('LUI', 'b'),\n    ]\n    s = s.replace('  logic [31:0] alu_result;\\\\n  alu u_alu (', '  logic [31:0] alu_result;\\\\n  alu_terms u_alu (')\n    s = s.replace('    .op  (in.ctrl.alu_op),', '''    .op  (in.ctrl.alu_op),\n    .enable (is_alu_result),''')\n    s = s.replace('({32{is_alu_result}} & alu_result) |','alu_result |')\n    alu = rtl / 'alu.sv'\n    alu.write_text(alu.read_text()+'''\n/* verilator lint_off DECLFILENAME */\nmodule alu_terms (\n  input logic [4:0] op,\n  input logic [31:0] a, b,\n  input logic enable,\n  output logic [31:0] out\n);\n  assign out =\n''' + ' |\\\\n'.join(f'    ({{32{{enable && op == ALU_{op}}}}} & ({expr}))' for op,expr in ops) + ''';\nendmodule\n/* verilator lint_on DECLFILENAME */\n''')\nif 'fallback' in opts:\n    pkg = rtl / 'core_pkg.sv'\n    pkg.write_text(pkg.read_text().replace('    logic [31:0] rs2_val;\\\\n    logic [31:0] imm;', '    logic [31:0] rs2_val;\\\\n    logic [31:0] alu_b_fallback;\\\\n    logic [31:0] imm;',1))\n    id_file = rtl / 'id_stage.sv'\n    id_file.write_text(id_file.read_text().replace('      reg_q.rs2_val  <= rs2_data;', '      reg_q.rs2_val  <= rs2_data;\\\\n      reg_q.alu_b_fallback <= dec_alu_src ? imm : rs2_data;'))\n    s = s.replace('({32{\"'!in.ctrl.alu_src && fwd_rs2_sel[0]}} & in.rs2_val) |'\"\\\\n                 ({32{in.ctrl.alu_src}} & in.imm)', '({32{in.ctrl.alu_src || fwd_rs2_sel[0]}} & in.alu_b_fallback)')\nif 'predecode' in opts:\n    s = s.replace('    .op  (in.ctrl.alu_op),\\\\n    .enable (is_alu_result),','    .select_op (in.alu_selects),')\n    s = s.replace('  logic        is_alu_result, m_active;', '  logic        m_active;')\n    s = s.replace('  assign is_alu_result = \"'!(is_mul || is_div || in.ctrl.is_jump || in.ctrl.is_auipc);'\"\\\\n', '')\n    pkg = rtl / 'core_pkg.sv'\n    pkg.write_text(pkg.read_text().replace('    logic [31:0] imm;', '    logic [31:0] imm;\\\\n    logic [10:0] alu_selects;',1))\n    id_file = rtl / 'id_stage.sv'\n    selects = \\\"      for (int op = 0; op < 11; op++)\\\\n        reg_q.alu_selects[op] <= \"'!dec_is_jump && !dec_is_auipc && dec_alu_op == 5'\"'(op);\\\"\n    id_file.write_text(id_file.read_text().replace('      reg_q.imm      <= imm;', '      reg_q.imm      <= imm;\\\\n'+selects))\n    alu = rtl / 'alu.sv'\n    t = alu.read_text().replace('  input logic [4:0] op,', '  input logic [10:0] select_op,').replace('  input logic enable,\\\\n','')\n    for i,(op,_) in enumerate(ops):\n        t = t.replace(f'enable && op == ALU_{op}}}', f'select_op[{i}]}}')\n    alu.write_text(t)\nif 'addr' in opts:\n    s = s.replace('  assign rs1_plus_imm    = rs1 + in.imm;', '  assign rs1_plus_imm    = rs1 + alu_b;')\n    s = s.replace('    .out (alu_result)', '    .out (alu_result)')\nif 'branch' in opts:\n    s = s.replace('  always_comb begin\\\\n    case (in.ctrl.branch_op)', '''  logic branch_lt, branch_signed_lt;\n  logic [3:0] branch_lt_byte, branch_eq_byte;\n  for (genvar lane = 0; lane < 4; lane++) begin : gen_compare\n    assign branch_lt_byte[lane] = rs1[8*lane +: 8] < rs2[8*lane +: 8];\n    assign branch_eq_byte[lane] = rs1[8*lane +: 8] == rs2[8*lane +: 8];\n  end\n  assign branch_lt = branch_lt_byte[3] |\n                    (branch_eq_byte[3] & branch_lt_byte[2]) |\n                    ((&branch_eq_byte[3:2]) & branch_lt_byte[1]) |\n                    ((&branch_eq_byte[3:1]) & branch_lt_byte[0]);\n  assign branch_signed_lt = (rs1[31] \"'^ rs2[31]) ? rs1[31] : branch_lt;\n  always_comb begin\n    case (in.ctrl.branch_op)'\"''')\n    for orig,new in [\n     ('\"'$signed(rs1) <  $signed(rs2)'\"','branch_signed_lt'),\n     ('\"'$signed(rs1) >= $signed(rs2)'\"','\"'!branch_signed_lt'\"'),\n     ('rs1 <  rs2','branch_lt'), ('rs1 >= rs2','\"'!branch_lt'\"'),\n     ('rs1 == rs2','&branch_eq_byte'), ('rs1 \"'!= rs2'\"','\"'!(&branch_eq_byte)'\"')]:\n        s = s.replace(orig,new)\nex.write_text(s)\nPY\npython3 \\\"\"'$scratch/fast_ex.py\" ex_gate_branch gate branch\npython3 \"$scratch/fast_ex.py\" ex_fallback fallback\npython3 \"$scratch/fast_ex.py\" ex_fuse gate merge predecode\npython3 \"$scratch/fast_ex.py\" ex_addr addr\npython3 \"$scratch/fast_ex.py\" ex_merge merge'", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
