/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}, 'perturbations': [[0, 45.298, 15], [1, 47.542, 15], [2, 47.542, 15]], 'logic_levels': 15} - 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-001-r2s0 (regression, +5.23%): Driving fetch directly from the registered EX/MEM redirect target while invalidating the younger EX slot preserved CoreMark's cycle count and removed the EX-to-IF-to-ID redirect path from Gowin's worst paths, leaving the register-file-to-data-memory path through the EX ALU to cap median Fmax at 47.542 MHz.\n{'id': 'hyp-20261120-001-r3s0', 'fitness': 129.58, 'cycles': 425543\n…[3505 of 6577 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:b1d63a2626c3c8ba]…\nLU enables, and divisor-width flags removed late decode from wide mux paths and raised median Gowin Fmax to 76.909 MHz at unchanged CoreMark cycles, with the divider byte prefix and forwarded branch target limiting different placements.\n{'id': 'hyp-20261120-002-r6s1', 'fitness': 192.85, 'cycles': 4015275, 'fmax_mhz': 77.436, 'critical_path': {'from': 'cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs1_val_8_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_if/recovering_s1', 'slack_ns': -8.32, 'arrival_ns': 18.614, 'logic_cells': 33, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu', 'cpu/u_ex']}, 'perturbations': [[0, 75.075, 14], [1, 77.436, 15], [2, 77.436, 15]], 'logic_levels': 14} - 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-002-r6s1 (improvement, +12.40%): Checking the resolved successor against the FIFO head PC (fetch PC when empty) lets a four-entry fall-through LUT RAM queue absorb ready fetches during backend holds without storing predicted successors, cutting stalled CoreMark cycles by 6.91% and reaching 77.436 MHz median Gowin Fmax with the recovery mux after its candidate registers.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
