{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg 'hyp-20261120-001-r6s0|hyp-20261120-002-r6s1|hyp-20261120-001-r5s0' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python -c 'import json,sys; [print(r[\\\"id\\\"],r.get(\\\"hypothesis\\\",{}).get(\\\"hypothesis\\\"),r.get(\\\"implementation_notes\\\",\\\"\\\"),sep=\\\"\\\\n\\\") for r in map(json.loads,sys.stdin)]'\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261120-001-r5s0\nShorten the arithmetic paths into and out of EX/MEM without adding a\nstage or a bubble. Select the extended load value or the EX register\nresult before the MEM/WB edge and latch one final write value. Drive\nwriteback and MEM/WB forwarding directly from that register. When\ndmem stalls, hold the registered value, destination tag, and forwarding\neligibility while clearing retirement valid. A held consumer can then\nstill forward from a producer that retired during the stall.\n\nTap the raw forwarded rs1 plus immediate sum already computed for JALR\nand register it as the full 32-bit effective address under the existing\nEX/MEM hold. Preserve bit zero for the byte address and clear it only\nfor the JALR target. Use the effective address for the bus, alignment,\nload extraction, store masks, and RVFI. Select the ALU, link, multiply,\nand divide register results with parallel one-hot masks driven by\ndecoded operation type. Apply EX validity, stalls, and traps to the\nside-effect controls and M-unit handshakes. Preserve the predictor,\nforwarding priority, memory handshakes, and single-channel retirement.\n\nShorten the divider feedback with one exact parallel radix-16 digit\nper work edge, following the radix change exercised in r4s1. After\ncapturing operand magnitudes,\nconsume the top byte on the first work edge. Use a four-bit quotient\nand remainder lookup for the first nibble and a parallel narrow trial\nsubtraction for the second nibble. Only divisors through 15 and 255\nrespectively can change those prefixes. Prepare the wide odd divisor\nmultiples on that same edge and derive even multiples by left shifts.\nFor each of the six remaining nibbles, subtract the fifteen 36-bit\nmultiples in parallel, including a 37th bit for borrow. Adjacent borrow\nflags select the difference for the largest fitting multiple or the\ntrial itself for digit zero. Shift the digit into the quotient and\nregister the selected remainder. Correct the sign on the held result\nduring the valid cycle. The result still transfers eight rising e\n…[13681 of 16753 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:14e4f193f68460f6]…\nVerilator lint, all 84 cocotb cases across seven runners, and `make cosim TARGET=bench NRET=1` passed. Selftest and the three random programs matched the ISS with and without stalls. Stalled CoreMark validated the canonical CRCs (`e9f5`, `e714`, `1fd7`, `8e3a`, `fcaf`) in 4,015,275 marked cycles with no out-of-bounds access.\n- Gowin placed the final RTL at 75.075, 77.436, and 77.436 MHz. The 77.436 MHz median and measured cycle count give 192.85 iterations/s, 12.4% above the champion. Option 0 used 5,049 logic cells and its longest reported path reached the IF recovery register from EX. Options 1 and 2 were divider-limited.\n- `bash formal/run_all.sh` passed all 53 single-retirement ALTOPS checks after one fix. The first `pc_fwd_ch0` counterexample retired a buffered instruction at PC 0 after its predecessor reported 0x14 as the successor. Yosys had lowered the packed-struct array incorrectly. The explicit vector memory fixed the failure. The register-consistency proof took about 20 minutes on the final RTL.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
