{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_47", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"scratch=/srv/hwebench/tmp/4876824c/37f9e798/r7s0-research\nrg -o 'DONE \\\\([A-Z]+' \\\"\"'$scratch/carry/formal/progress.log\" | sort | uniq -c\nrg '\"'DONE.*(liveness|FAIL)|liveness.*DONE' \\\"\"'$scratch/carry/formal/progress.log\" | tail -6\ncat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-001-r7s0.yaml\ndate -u'", "aggregated_output": "     20 DONE (PASS\nSBY  7:44:36 [liveness_ch0] DONE (PASS, rc=0)\nid: hyp-20261120-001-r7s0\ntitle: \"Move arithmetic selection off the execute feedback paths\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The champion takes 4,015,275 marked cycles at 77.436 MHz. Gowin's\n  median placement puts the divider byte prefix and ID/EX forwarding\n  into the integer result register within 1 ps of each other. Another\n  placement is limited by the forwarded JALR sum into recovery. Round 6\n  registered arithmetic selects but left the prefix and target paths\n  near the timing limit. Clearing the acceptance margin at the current\n  cycle count requires more than 81.0 MHz median.\nhypothesis: |\n  Shorten the arithmetic feedback paths without adding a pipeline edge.\n  Register the final one-hot forwarding and ALU operand masks in ID/EX.\n  Qualify producer tags with the write eligibility of the values about\n  to enter EX/MEM and MEM/WB. Use the live EX slot's write intent and\n  link alignment, and MEM's write intent after load alignment. Give\n  EX/MEM priority and retain the masks with a held consumer. Keep raw\n  register operand masks for branches, stores, M requests and RVFI.\n  Register one-hot integer result enables and OR the enabled integer\n  terms directly with the link and M results.\n\n  Compute JALR successor agreement in parallel with the effective address\n  sum. For bit 1, the carry from bit 0 is rs1[0] AND imm[0]. For each\n  higher bit the required carry is rs1 XOR imm XOR the candidate PC at\n  that bit. Check the required carries in parallel against the carry\n  implied by the previous bit's operands and candidate sum. Reduce the\n  checks over bits 1 through 31, ignoring bit 0 and carry out of bit 31.\n  Keep the raw 32-bit sum for memory and target capture, the JALR bit-1\n  alignment check, and the existing redirect and training edge.\n\n  In the divider, begin first-nibble work at request capture. Derive the\n  top four dividend magnitude bits from the raw operand, signedness and\n  a lower-28-bits-zero check. Derive the low four divisor\n…[1056 of 4128 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:43b7a9b5aa9cb213]…\nected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Use the existing forward unit before the ID/EX edge and capture the one-hot producer, PC and immediate operand masks and integer operation enables with each consumer.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire next-producer qualification and registered selects while preserving the nret=1 interface.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Expose MEM's current write eligibility including the load alignment check.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Use registered masks, combine integer and link/M results, and check JALR agreement with parallel local carry constraints.\"\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Expose a one-hot integer datapath for EX and retain the standalone encoded ALU interface.\"\n  - file: rtl/div_unit.sv\n    description: \"Capture the first-nibble result and byte cutoff at launch so only the second prefix digit feeds the first work edge.\"\nFri Nov 20 06:46:40 UTC 2026\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_48","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"set -e\nscratch=/srv/hwebench/tmp/4876824c/37f9e798/r7s0-research\npython - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nsuite = Path('/srv/hwebench/tmp/4876824c/37f9e798/r7s0-research/carry/test')\np=suite/'test_pipeline.py'\ns=p.read_text()\ns=s.replace('''@cocotb.test()\nasync def warmed_jalr_wraps_and_clears_low_bit(dut):\n    jalr = JALR(1, 5, 0x23)\n    program = {\n        0x00: ADDI(5, 0, -2),''','''@cocotb.test()\n@cocotb.parametrize(operands=[(-1, 0x21), (-2, 0x23), (0x42, -0x22)])\nasync def warmed_jalr_wraps_and_clears_low_bit(dut, operands):\n    base, offset = operands\n    jalr = JALR(1, 5, offset)\n    program = {\n        0x00: ADDI(5, 0, base),''')\np.write_text(s)\np=suite/'test_div_unit.py'\ns=p.read_text()\ns=s.replace('async def _check_result(dut, op, a, b, expected):',\n            'async def _check_result(dut, op, a, b, expected, *, change_after_launch=False):')\ns=s.replace('''    dut.request_valid.value = 0\n\n    for _ in range(7):''','''    dut.request_valid.value = 0\n    if change_after_launch:\n        dut.op.value = ALU_REMU\n        dut.a.value = (~a) & MASK32\n        dut.b.value = (~b) & MASK32\n\n    for _ in range(7):''')\ndivider_test=s.rsplit('@cocotb.test()',1)[1]\ns=s.rsplit('@cocotb.test()',1)[0]+'@cocotb.test()'+divider_test.replace('a, b, quotient)', 'a, b, quotient, change_after_launch=True)').replace('a, b, remainder)', 'a, b, remainder, change_after_launch=True)')\np.write_text(s)\nPY\ncd \\\"\"'$scratch/carry\"\npytest -q -p no:cacheprovider --rootdir=. test/test_pipeline.py test/test_div_unit.py'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
