ion's 4,015,275\\nmarked cycles and lowered median Fmax. A scratch predictor that\\nreplayed the predicted instruction stream saved 256,703 marked cycles\\nwith canonical CRCs.\\n\", 'hypothesis': 'Extend the tagged last-successor predictor with 32 learned streams of\\nup to 16 contiguous instruction words each. On acceptance of a fetch\\nwith a full BTB hit, open a stream at the predicted successor,\\nincluding a predicted fall-through. Index the stream by XORing word\\naddress bits [6:2] and [11:7], and tag it with [31:7]. Register the\\nindex and tag at launch and track the word offset as requests\\nadvance. Cl\n…[1671 of 4743 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:f17b4cb1b858a3dc]…\n for the same row first, while replay uses the committed prefix and payload.\n\nReady responses retain the empty-queue decode bypass. Replay enqueues during instruction-bus stalls. Every accepted fetch writes the free FIFO slot, including a bypass, which leaves the pointers unchanged. A dequeue from a full FIFO makes its slot available the following cycle.\n\nQueue discard uses the registered pending-target flag. It exposes the corrected PC immediately and rebases the read pointer to the write pointer on the next edge. This removes the direct EX redirect path to the queue pointers while giving the corrected e\ntimestamp 2026-11-20T08:09:48.351227Z\nslot 2\nround_id 7\nlesson - 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-003-r7s2 (improvement, +9.39%): Replaying learned BTB successor words during instruction-bus stalls cut CoreMark cycles by 6.39%, and writing every accepted word into a FIFO slot free at cycle start, even on decode bypass, removed decode acceptance from the RAM write enable and helped reach 79.292 MHz median Gowin Fmax.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
