{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_28", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor x in map(json.loads,Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines()):\n if x['id'] in ('hyp-20261120-002-r8s1','hyp-20261120-002-r6s1'):\n  print(x['id'])\n  print(x['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261120-002-r6s1\nPut a four-entry circular fall-through FIFO between instruction memory\nand decode. Each entry holds the full PC and instruction word in\nasynchronous-read, synchronous-write distributed RAM. Track read and\nwrite pointers with wrap bits, resetting only the queue state. Advance\nthe fetch PC only when a ready response can bypass to decode or enter\nthe queue. A full queue can pop and refill on the same edge. Decode\nalways uses the oldest buffered entry when one exists and can issue\nit while imem is stalled. Feed the existing load-use and backend\ninterlocks with this selected word and its availability.\n\nVerify each advancing EX instruction against the PC of the oldest\nunissued instruction. That is the FIFO head when occupied and the\ncurrent fetch address when empty, even if imem is waiting. Enqueuing\ninto an empty queue during an EX hold preserves this PC because the\nnew head has the prior fetch address. This removes the need to\npropagate a second PC through each FIFO entry and ID/EX.\n\nRegister the two recovery candidates separately in IF. One is PC+4.\nThe other is the relative target or the JALR sum with bit zero cleared,\nselected by decoded instruction type. Register the resolved choice\nalongside them and select the recovery PC after the edge. Keep\nfull-width comparison and the existing alignment and trap behavior\nin EX. Use the registered candidates, choice and paired training PC\nfor a one-edge-deferred table write. Retain the tagged last-successor\npolicy, including training conditional fall-through.\n\nOn a valid EX redirect, reset both FIFO pointers regardless of\nconcurrent push or pop and annul the younger ID/EX slot. Track issuing\nthe target fetch separately from issuing that corrected instruction\ninto ID/EX. Fetch can resume from the corrected stream as soon as the\ntarget response is bypassed or buffered. Keep EX squash active until\nthe corrected instruction is accepted by ID/EX. Hold the registered\ntarget while imem is stalled, and apply the same discard and refetch\nbehavior to FENCE.I at P\n…[1876 of 4948 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:4f18a24aa20d0939]…\ndex and\nentry alongside the synchronous read and forward the captured write\nwhen the two indices coincide. This gives deterministic replay across\nthe block RAM's read-during-write cases. A pending redirect selects\nthe corrected external fetch and disables replay until an accepted\nword has realigned the replay read with the fetch PC. On reset and\nthe existing non-training redirect invalidation, including FENCE.I,\ngate replay immediately and scrub the packed valid bits through the\nRAM write port while external fetch keeps running. Apply reset and\ninvalidation before admitting subsequent fills.\n\nA scratch 512-entry version passed the canonical CoreMark CRCs in\n3,540,112 marked cycles, down 5.81%. Gowin used 5,305 logic cells\nand six block RAMs including the wrapper's original four. Its\n77.493 MHz median yielded 218.90 iter/sec. This cycle count needs\na median above 78.12 MHz to clear the 4.6% acceptance margin.\nThe clock target is 79 MHz. The existing EX recovery and divider\npaths limited different placements.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom shutil import copytree\norig_dir=Path.cwd()/'cores/bench/rtl'\nroot=Path('/srv/hwebench/tmp/4876824c/4ece65a7/bench-r9-protos-ks1k0g5j')\nfile='ex_stage.sv'\nsource=(orig_dir/file).read_text()\ni=source.index('  always_comb begin\\\\n    case (in.ctrl.branch_op)')\nj=source.index('  assign pc_plus4',i)\nfor width in (4,8,16):\n rows=32//width\n code=f'''  logic [{rows-1}:0] chunk_eq, chunk_lt;\n  logic unsigned_lt, signed_lt, equal;\n  for (genvar chunk = 0; chunk < {rows}; chunk++) begin : gen_branch_compare\n    assign chunk_eq[chunk] = rs1[chunk*{width} +: {width}] == rs2[chunk*{width} +: {width}];\n    assign chunk_lt[chunk] = rs1[chunk*{width} +: {width}] < rs2[chunk*{width} +: {width}];\n  end\n  assign equal = &chunk_eq;\n  assign unsigned_lt = '''+' |\\\\n                       '.join(f'chunk_lt[{k}]' if k==rows-1 else f'(chunk_lt[{k}] && (&chunk_eq[{rows-1}:{k+1}]))' for k in reversed(range(rows)))+''';\n  assign signed_lt = (rs1[31] \"'^ rs2[31]) ? rs1[31] : unsigned_lt;\n  assign branch_cond = (in.ctrl.branch_op[2] ? (in.ctrl.branch_op[1] ? unsigned_lt : signed_lt)\n                                             : equal) ''^ in.ctrl.branch_op[0];\n\n'\"'''\n name=f'branch{width}'\n copytree(orig_dir,root/name)\n (root/name/file).write_text(source[:i]+code+source[j:])\n  # The validated branch funct3 set is maintained by ID.\nPY\npython3 - <<'PY'\nfrom concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom tools.eval.gowin import build, summarize\nwt=Path.cwd()\nroot=Path('/srv/hwebench/tmp/4876824c/4ece65a7/bench-r9-protos-ks1k0g5j')\nnames=('branch4','branch8','branch16')\nwith ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=4) as pool:\n futures={name:[pool.submit(build,wt,root/name,'fpga/core_bench_si.sv',opt,root/'reports'/name/str(opt)) for opt in (0,1)] for name in names}\n for name, fs in futures.items():\n  for job in fs:\n   run=job.result()\n   print(name, run['place_option'], run.get('fmax_mhz'), run.get('logic'),run.get('critical_paths',[])[:3], flush=True)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
