e while waiting and advances the divide once through the\\nexisting EX/MEM forwarding and retirement path when its result is available.\\nThe result stays valid until EX/MEM accepts it. Fast ALU operations and MUL*\\nretain their current latency. The launch, six computation cycles, and advance\\noccupy eight EX cycles for every divide or remainder, including special\\ncases. The seven added cycles leave room for a redirect or load-use bubble\\nin the existing ten-cycle formal liveness window. Use the existing ALTOPS\\nvalues with the same transaction latency and hold protocol so the formal\\ngate still exercise\n…[10785 of 13857 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:849bc7b263364d1e]…\nge.sv', 'description': 'Capture late branch metadata when the older load completes, keep the ordinary branch path for other instructions, and annul younger side effects on a late mismatch.'}, {'file': 'rtl/mem_stage.sv', 'description': 'Stage the late branch completion in MEM/WB and keep it in order across the registered correction, releasing it once.'}, {'file': 'rtl/if_stage.sv', 'description': 'Register the late correction, arbitrate separately captured predictor updates, and preserve the replay scrub rule while isolating RAM writes from the late verdict.'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Cover BEQ and BNE after stalled LB, LH and LW producers, a misaligned producer, both operands matching the load, and a changed branch direction followed by DIV with wrong-path stores and M-unit launches suppressed.'}, {'file': 'test/test_if_stage.py', 'description': 'Initialize the late correction and training inputs and exercise queue discard and a held late redirect across instruction-bus stalls.'}]}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
