{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg 'r9s2|r8s1|r9s0' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python -c 'import sys,json\nfor l in sys.stdin:\n d=json.loads(l); print(d[\\\"id\\\"]); print(d[\\\"critical_path\\\"]); print(d.get(\\\"perturbations\\\")); print(d[\\\"implementation_notes\\\"][-8000:])'\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261120-002-r8s1\n{'from': 'cpu/u_if/take_target_q_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_if/replay_replay_0_1_s', 'slack_ns': -7.852, 'arrival_ns': 18.147, 'logic_cells': 28, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_if']}\n[[0, 77.808, 11], [1, 83.921, 12], [2, 83.921, 12]]\n\nhyp-20261120-001-r9s0\n{'from': 'cpu/u_mem/reg_q.write_result_14_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_div/dividend_quotient_q_28_s1', 'slack_ns': -7.499, 'arrival_ns': 17.793, 'logic_cells': 14, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_div']}\n[[0, 80.009, 13], [1, 84.28, 13], [2, 84.28, 13]]\n# Load-dependent equality branches\n\n- Aligned BEQ and BNE use a load-to-branch bypass. Decode still interlocks other load users. EX qualifies register producers using the effective address alignment and records the forwarding selects. A trapping load leaves the branch free to use the older writer.\n- EX checks both full-width successor PCs and incorporates BEQ/BNE polarity into the saved match bits. MEM selects the result using a dedicated register for the width- and sign-extended load value at the MEM/WB boundary. An older miss suppresses younger memory and RV32M requests and takes priority in fetch recovery. Late branches train the predictor on misses, leaving the port available for EX when a late prediction is correct.\n- Decode registers the one-hot forwarding and ALU operand masks. Fetch reuses the late branch's already captured successor candidates for recovery. The MEM match result drives recovery control without a path from the dmem response through the EX forwarding mux.\n- The first formal run found a bounded-liveness counterexample when a late miss targeted a divide. The branch now completes retirement while IF presents the registered recovery address. The corrected path issues on the same edge as before, and the divider keeps its existing schedule. Directed tests cover this sequence, predictor arbitration, held subword loads, both branch polarities, both sources matching, trapping loads, and wrong-path stores and RV32M requests.\n\n## Local validation\n\n- Verilator lint passed.\n-\n…[1861 of 4933 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:134ab56cd783720a]…\nalls, full source tagging, and invalidation with either a stalled or ready bus.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator lint passed without warnings. All eight cocotb runners passed.\n- Co-simulation passed for selftest and three random-trace ELFs with and without bus stalls. Stalled CoreMark passed all five canonical CRC checks and reported 3,540,112 marked cycles.\n- Gowin placement options 0, 1, and 2 reached 75.051, 86.171, and 86.171 MHz. The median gives 243.41 CoreMark iterations/sec, 2.68% above the cited champion and below the 87.783 MHz acceptance threshold. Placement option 0 used 5,369 logic cells, 1,047 registers, and six block RAMs. Options 1 and 2 were limited by replay collision forwarding through instruction delivery and register-file reads into ID.\n- Local single-channel ALTOPS formal was incomplete within the implementation window. The one run passed 52 of 53 checks. Bitwuzla was still solving step 20 of `reg_ch0` and produced no counterexample. There were no formal-driven RTL fixes or retries.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
