{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_14", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -i 'load.use bubbles|coremark.*profile|MULs|replay cycles|empty.*fetch' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl -o | sort | uniq -c\nls -ld /opt/gowin /opt/hwe-toolchain/*\"", "aggregated_output": "      1 CoreMark iter/sec. Its\\n199.837 ns worst path spans 156 cells from MEM/WB through forwarding and the\\nEX ALU. The variable signed and unsigned division and remainder expressions\\nare the likely source of that depth. They feed the shared ALU result used for\\ndata addresses, so their timing cost applies even when CoreMark is executing\\na load, store, or integer instruction. The baseline Verilator trace under\\nthe scored stall settings retired zero DIV, DIVU, REM, or REMU instructions\\nin the 4,491,485-cycle marked CoreMark window. The run passed the canonical\\nCRC checks.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The Gowin baseline reaches 5.442 MHz and 12.12 CoreMark iter/sec. Its\\n199.837 ns worst path spans 156 cells from MEM/WB through forwarding and the\\nEX ALU. The variable signed and unsigned division and remainder expressions\\nare the likely source of that depth. They feed the shared ALU result used for\\ndata addresses, so their timing cost applies even when CoreMark is executing\\na load, store, or integer instruction. The baseline Verilator trace under\\nthe scored stall settings retired zero DIV, DIVU, REM, or REMU instructions\\nin the 4,491,485-cycle marked CoreMark window. The run passed the canonical\\nCRC checks.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU onto one registered restoring divider. Capture\\nunsigned operand magnitudes and sign flags at launch. Reuse six cascaded\\nradix-2 steps per cycle for six cycles, shifting in a 36-bit zero-extended\\ndividend. Each step uses a 33-bit trial subtract and selects the updated\\nremainder by borrow. Select and sign-correct the quotient or remainder from\\nthe final registered state. Return all ones for division by zero and the\\noriginal dividend for remainder by zero. Signed magnitude arithmetic must\\nreturn INT_MIN and zero for the overflow quotient and remainder respectively.\\n\\nA divide holds fetch and ID/EX while older memory and writeback work drains.\\nEX issues a bubble while waiting and advances the divide once through the\\nexisting EX/MEM forwardi\n…[68951 of 72023 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:07f42092655b0e09]…\nt available the following cycle.\\n\\nQueue discard uses the registered pending-target flag. It exposes the corrected PC immediately and rebases the read pointer to the write pointer on the next edge. This removes the direct EX redirect path to the queue pointers while giving the corrected external response the same bypass or enqueue behavior. The pending-target flag masks replay and new fill captures. Redirects without predictor training register a global invalidation pulse with priority over stream validity writes.\\n\\nThe pipeline tests cover the 16-word limit on a predicted fall-through, row collisions and contiguous replacement, a redirect with replayed stores queued, and refetch\n      3 load-use bubbles\ndrwxr-xr-x  5 nobody nogroup 4096 Sep 28 05:13 /opt/gowin\ndrwxr-xr-x  2 nobody nogroup 4096 Sep 28 02:44 /opt/hwe-toolchain/bin\ndrwxr-xr-x 12 nobody nogroup 4096 Apr 24  2026 /opt/hwe-toolchain/oss-cad-suite\ndrwxr-xr-x 10 nobody nogroup 4096 Oct 23  2025 /opt/hwe-toolchain/xpack-riscv-none-elf-gcc-15.2.0-1\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
