{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg 'r11s[012]' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import json,sys; print(\\\"\\\\n\\\".join(json.dumps({k:e.get(k) for k in (\\\"id\\\",\\\"title\\\",\\\"category\\\",\\\"fitness\\\",\\\"fmax_mhz\\\",\\\"cycles\\\",\\\"seeds\\\",\\\"perturbations\\\",\\\"critical_path\\\",\\\"implementation_notes\\\")},ensure_ascii=False)[:9500] for e in map(json.loads,sys.stdin) if \\\"r11\\\" in e[\\\"id\\\"]))'\"", "aggregated_output": "{\"id\": \"hyp-20261120-001-r11s0\", \"title\": \"Register the independent EX recovery decisions before fetch\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"fitness\": 249.15, \"fmax_mhz\": 88.203, \"cycles\": 3540112, \"seeds\": [86.671, 88.203, 88.203], \"perturbations\": [[0, 86.671, 10], [1, 88.203, 10], [2, 88.203, 10]], \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_if/correction_pending_q_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_if/pc_q_7_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -6.538, \"arrival_ns\": 16.832, \"logic_cells\": 11, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_if\"]}, \"implementation_notes\": \"# Bench EX recovery\\n\\nEX compares both candidate next PCs against the oldest unissued full PC. IF registers the two advance-qualified misses, the aligned direction, and the selected word PC. IF can issue a ready correction on the first recovery cycle and holds the address during imem backpressure. The recovery state squashes the younger EX slot until decode issues the corrected instruction. FENCE.I forces both misses, and a registered redirect without predictor training starts the replay scrub.\\n\\nThe tagged successor table stores replay-index and full word-PC equality with each successor. On each accepted lookahead read, IF captures the collision decisions using the actual fill enable. An exact collision forwards the accepted bus word. A different tag at the same index blocks the old RAM result. A ready bus response still has priority and the queue issues in FIFO order.\\n\\nID registers the one-hot bypass masks after checking both incoming producers' write enables. The younger eligible producer takes priority. ID captures PC or the register-file value for ALU A and the immediate or register-file value for ALU B. EX uses the raw forwarded operands for branches, stores, RV32M, and RVFI. Directed tests cover both recovery directions, imem and dmem holds, replay collisions, FENCE.I, AUIPC, and trapping producers.\\n\\nThe recovery hold uses dmem backpressure once the corrected word arrives. Squashing EX disables the load-use and M-extension stalls during recovery. The predictor uses a full-width XNOR reduction for tag \n…[6649 of 9721 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:7405554076609f76]…\nt step 20 near the implementation deadline. Unchanged proof input also reached the six-minute diagnostic limit with Boolector and Yices. No run produced a counterexample, and no formal fixes were needed for the completed checks.\\n- `make cosim TARGET=bench NRET=1` passed for selftest and all three random programs with both zero-wait and stalled buses. CoreMark completed ten iterations in 3,489,128 marked cycles, a 1.44% reduction, with the required CRCs and validation banner.\\n- `make fpga TARGET=bench NRET=1` reported 249.64 iterations/sec, 5.31% above the champion and above the 247.96 acceptance threshold. Gowin options 0, 1, and 2 reached 82.049, 87.101, and 87.101 MHz. Option 0 used 5,823 logic cells and six block RAMs. The median critical path is EX forwarding into the ALU result register.\\n\\nDirection counters are shared by sources that hash to the same row. Corrected transfers with a nonsequential successor can need a second redirect. Both cases are covered by EX's full-width successor validation.\\n\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
