{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_97", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,180p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-002-r12s1.yaml; git status --short\"", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261120-002-r12s1\ntitle: \"Move operand interlocks across the issue register\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The bench champion scores 249.64 CoreMark iterations per second at\n  87.101 MHz over 3,489,128 marked cycles. A repeat of Gowin option 1\n  found nearly tied paths into the EX result register and the fetch\n  FIFO head register. The latter runs from the fetch PC through replay\n  selection and the incoming instruction's load-use test. Earlier\n  load bypass experiments saved bubbles but added poorly timed paths\n  between the memory, execute, and recovery stages. A registered\n  operand interlock can break that feedback while keeping the existing\n  load latency and the memory response behind MEM/WB.\nhypothesis: |\n  Use ID/EX as a one-entry issue slot that can accept a consumer just\n  behind a load. On admission, register its nonzero source matches\n  against the two older destinations. Qualify the older match with\n  MEM's alignment-checked write intent on the edge that advances that\n  producer into MEM/WB. EX then uses the registered older match\n  directly for forwarding, with the actual EX/MEM write enable still\n  qualifying the younger match and giving it priority.\n\n  Check load-use in the registered issue slot against EX/MEM's load\n  status and the stored matches. Suppress EX advance and M-unit launch\n  for a waiting consumer. Keep the entry and its selects stable while\n  dmem is stalled. On the edge that transfers the load into MEM/WB,\n  copy any matching value from the departing MEM/WB producer into the\n  held entry's fallback operands. Clear the EX/MEM matches and assign\n  the affected sources to MEM/WB when the load can write. A misaligned\n  load traps, and its consumer uses the preserved older architectural\n  value. Then execute the consumer through the ordinary forwarding path.\n\n  Drive decode readiness from the registered slot's interlock and the\n  existing backend holds. Fetch queue pop and head promotion no longer\n  depend on the replayed word's register fields in the same cycle.\n  Preserve the full-width oldest-unissued-PC check, the registered\n  redirect and squash, and the ready correction path. An EX slot held\n  for a load must produce no memory operation, training, or RVFI event.\n  Keep single-channel in-order retirement and the current M-unit and\n  ALTOPS schedules. Verify an adjacent dependent consumer with an\n  independent source from the departing WB producer, a trapping load,\n  and a stalled load followed by a dependent branch or DIV.\n\n  A scratch build passed ISS cosim and the canonical stalled CoreMark\n  CRCs at 3,489,128 marked cycles. Gowin options 0, 1, and 2 reached\n  86.762, 88.585, and 88.585 MHz. The median gives 253.89 iterations\n  per second, a 1.7% gain. The new median limit runs from a registered\n  MEM/WB match through the forwarded branch comparison into recovery.\n  The acceptance margin needs a median above 91.11 MHz at this cycle\n  count.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 2\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire producer write eligibility, the registered issue-slot matches, the EX load wait, and the load completion edge used to update the held consumer.\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \"Capture the nonzero destination matches and qualify the older producer before registration. Preserve departing MEM/WB values and reassign matching sources when a held load completes.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Use registered consumer matches and EX/MEM load status for load-use backpressure. Allow decode to fill the issue slot before that interlock applies.\"\n  - file: rtl/forward_unit.sv\n    description: \"Use the already-qualified MEM/WB match when selecting one-hot forwarding sources. Give a write-enabled EX/MEM match priority.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Suppress EX advance and M-unit launch while a load-dependent consumer waits.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Export the alignment-qualified write intent for the entry transferring into MEM/WB.\"\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
