{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg 'r(12|13)s[012]' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | jq '{id,title,fmax_mhz,cycles,fitness,critical_path,implementation_notes,seeds}'\"", "aggregated_output": "{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20261120-001-r12s0\",\n  \"title\": \"Complete low-half multiplication in MEM\",\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 89.17,\n  \"cycles\": 3430915,\n  \"fitness\": 259.9,\n  \"critical_path\": {\n    \"from\": \"cpu/u_id/reg_q.fwd_rs1_1_s0\",\n    \"to\": \"cpu/u_if/invalidate_q_s0\",\n    \"slack_ns\": -6.226,\n    \"arrival_ns\": 16.521,\n    \"logic_cells\": 16,\n    \"modules\": [\n      \"clock_ibuf\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\",\n      \"cpu\",\n      \"cpu/u_if\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"implementation_notes\": \"# Complete low-half multiplication in MEM\\n\\nLow-half MUL captures the forwarded operands into the shared limb registers on the EX advance edge. EX/MEM carries the result marker and the original operand values. MEM adds the three relevant 16-bit terms with carry-save compression and a 16-bit final sum, then merges the product into the existing MEM/WB write value. Consecutive MULs can capture on consecutive edges. ALTOPS uses the same launch and MEM/WB timing. High-half products and division use their existing blocking transfer schedules. The core retires through the existing single RVFI channel.\\n\\nThe late-result interlock uses both raw source fields and ignores x0 destinations. ID registers EX/MEM and MEM/WB forwarding priorities from the incoming producers' post-trap write enables, with separate masks for ALU PC and immediate inputs. A dmem hold preserves the producer values and the consumer's masks. JAL and JALR use a zero integer ALU operation and merge the link in EX.\\n\\nThe timing work also split ordered branch comparisons into byte lanes, used carry-save equality for relative and sequential successors, and shortened the replay-to-ID path by registering same-row collisions and selecting the instruction sources in parallel.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- Verilator lint passed in real and ALTOPS builds. All 99 cocotb tests across eight suites passed. The arithmetic tests cover exact low and high products, consecutive capture edges, and the high-half handshake. Pipeline tests cover dependent and independent MULs, x0, mixed multiply and divide operations, both stages' trap ga\n…[10507 of 13579 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:fc9a3c68aeea7b75]…\ncles, a 2.69% reduction, with all five canonical CRCs and no out-of-bounds access.\\n- Gowin options 0, 1, and 2 completed at 84.410, 89.587, and 89.587 MHz. The median of 89.587 MHz yields 263.85 iterations/sec and falls short of the 93.329 MHz acceptance threshold. Replay and its issue feedback are the longest setup paths. The paired MEM ADD and store-data paths are outside the 25 longest setup paths in all three placements.\\n\",\n  \"seeds\": [\n    84.41,\n    89.587,\n    89.587\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20261120-003-r13s2\",\n  \"title\": \"Validate predicted load-dependent branches with registered rollback\",\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 86.39,\n  \"cycles\": 3357185,\n  \"fitness\": 257.33,\n  \"critical_path\": {\n    \"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_div/dividend_quotient_q_30_s1\",\n    \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_div/partial_remainder_q_4_s0\",\n    \"slack_ns\": -6.479,\n    \"arrival_ns\": 16.773,\n    \"logic_cells\": 41,\n    \"modules\": [\n      \"clock_ibuf\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex/u_div\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"implementation_notes\": \"\",\n  \"seeds\": [\n    87.119,\n    86.39,\n    86.39\n  ]\n}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg '\\\"category\\\"\\\\s*:\\\\s*\\\"structural\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | jq -r 'select(.id|test(\\\"r(4|6|8|9|10|11|12|13)s1\"'$\")) | [.id,.title,.fmax_mhz,(.critical_path|tostring),.implementation_notes] | @tsv'\"'\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261120-002-r4s1\tSeparate execute paths for memory and branch prediction\t66.022\t{\"from\":\"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s\",\"to\":\"cpu/u_if/recovering_s1\",\"slack_ns\":-10.741,\"arrival_ns\":21.035,\"logic_cells\":43,\"modules\":[\"clock_ibuf\",\"cpu/u_id\",\"cpu/u_ex\",\"cpu/u_if\"]}\t# Bench execute path separation\\n\\n## RTL and tests\\n\\n- EX/MEM registers the raw forwarded `rs1 + imm` sum under the existing data-memory hold. JALR masks bit zero only on its control-target path. MEM uses the registered address for the bus, alignment, byte lanes, load extraction and word-aligned RVFI reporting.\\n- IF samples the training source PC and pending bit alongside the existing recovery target. The next edge writes the tagged entry from the prior sampled pair. Reset clears pending training and entry validity. Fetch lookup and registered redirect timing retain the existing policy.\\n- The blocking divider uses a nibble lookup and a byte-wide trial on its prefix edge, then one parallel radix-16 digit on each of six edges. Odd multiples are prepared on the prefix edge from the captured divisor. Sign correction uses the held quotient or remainder, and the result still transfers eight edges after capture. ALTOPS retains its existing formulas and transfer timing.\\n- The directed tests cover every first nibble for divisors 0 through 16, quotient and remainder around the byte-prefix limit, a stalled byte store and dependent load using forwarded bases with negative offsets, and back-to-back training of distinct JAL and JALR successors.\\n\\n## Timing adjustments and results\\n\\nThe initial implementation reached 61.366 MHz median and was limited by the integer result path. EX now selects integer, link, multiply and divide results in parallel on the same writeback lane. EX also compares the relative and JALR candidates with the fetch PC, then selects the comparison result using the decoded target type. These changes shorten the result and redirect logic while retaining the existing forwarding priority and branch behavior.\\n\\nGowin placement options 0, 1 and\n…[16042 of 19114 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:fb1f71617658f89c]…\nainst the original divider.\\n- The initial formal run passed 52 of 53 checks. `reg_ch0` found an `LBU` writing x31 immediately before a trapping word whose raw rs1 field was x31. The implementation retains the load's raw-tag interlock and supplies raw RVFI tags that match a preceding low MUL or paired ADD from MEM/WB. The final ALTOPS run returned 52 passes, including liveness, ADD, MUL, and SW. `reg_ch0` remained unresolved within the local time budget in both the official Bitwuzla run and a separate Yices run of the same assertion.\\n- Stalled CoreMark completed in 3,395,412 marked cycles, a 2.69% reduction, with all five canonical CRCs and no out-of-bounds access.\\n- Gowin options 0, 1, and 2 completed at 84.410, 89.587, and 89.587 MHz. The median of 89.587 MHz yields 263.85 iterations/sec and falls short of the 93.329 MHz acceptance threshold. Replay and its issue feedback are the longest setup paths. The paired MEM ADD and store-data paths are outside the 25 longest setup paths in all three placements.\\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
