{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_45", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg '\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20261120-00[123]-r(9|10|12|13)s[012]\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | jq -r 'select(.id|test(\\\"r(9s0|10s0|10s1|13s1|13s2)\"'$\")) | [.id,.motivation,.hypothesis] | .[]'\"'\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261120-001-r9s0\nThe champion retired 135,320 BEQ/BNE instructions that immediately\nconsumed a load in the 3,540,112-cycle CoreMark interval. A scratch\ncombinational bypass passed the canonical CRCs in 3,406,310 cycles,\nbut reached only 58.434 MHz in Gowin placement option 1 because the\ndata memory path extended through EX into fetch recovery. Resolving\nthis branch in MEM can use the already registered load result while\neliminating the issue bubble.\n\n{\n  \"motivation\": \"The champion retired 135,320 BEQ/BNE instructions that immediately\\nconsumed a load in the 3,540,112-cycle CoreMark interval. A scratch\\ncombinational bypass passed the canonical CRCs in 3,406,310 cycles,\\nbut reached only 58.434 MHz in Gowin placement option 1 because the\\ndata memory path extended through EX into fetch recovery. Resolving\\nthis branch in MEM can use the already registered load result while\\neliminating the issue bubble.\\n\",\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Exempt aligned BEQ/BNE encodings from the adjacent load-use bubble.\\nUse the existing EX/MEM producer tag match to recognize the dependency\\nin EX. Qualify the producer's register-write eligibility before\\nlatching EX/MEM by checking alignment with the low two bits of the\\neffective address. This keeps the alignment check out of the ordinary\\nEX forwarding mux and lets a branch behind a trapping load use the\\nolder valid value. An unready load still holds EX through the existing\\ndmem stall. Retain the load-use interlock for other consumers.\\n\\nFor the bypassed branch, register its dependency bits, polarity and\\nother forwarded operand in EX/MEM. Compute its fall-through and\\nrelative target in EX, compare both against the oldest unissued PC,\\nand register the full-width match results with the candidates.\\nIn MEM, compare the saved operand to the older load's width- and\\nsign-extended value in MEM/WB. If both sources match the load tag,\\nthe equality predicate is true. Use the resulting branch condition\\nto select the precomputed match and resolved PC. A correct prediction\\nlets younger i\n…[24947 of 28019 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:07c713208e3808a9]…\nallback value, dependency bits, full successor candidates, and rejection bits in EX/MEM.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Check both successors, capture the branch-specific operands, and annul younger execution and cancel speculative M requests on a registered late miss.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/mem_stage.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Validate the late branch with the registered load or the saved fallback value, suppress younger bus effects and retirement on annulment, and report actual operands, traps and successors.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\",\n      \"description\": \"Predecode the bus and replay words, carry the bit through the queue, arbitrate registered recovery and training, and hold the older correction through backpressure.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\",\n      \"description\": \"Verify dependent branch forwarding, taken and fall-through rollback with stalls, FENCE.I, and cancellation of a younger store or divide.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
