{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_44", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"git status --short --untracked-files=all && git status --short --ignored=matching && sed -n '1,140p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261120-002-r3s1.yaml\"", "aggregated_output": "!! cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/\n!! cores/bench/generated/\n!! formal/riscv-formal\n!! test/cosim/__pycache__/\n!! tools/__pycache__/\n!! tools/eval/__pycache__/\nid: hyp-20261120-002-r3s1\ntitle: Isolate RV32M in a registered execute lane\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  The bench champion scores 117.93 CoreMark iter/sec at 49.767 MHz and\n  4,220,145 marked cycles. A fresh Gowin run traced the limiting paths in\n  all three placements through the unsigned multiplier DSP, ALU result\n  selection and data-memory BRAM address input. In the median placement,\n  the divider's three cascaded radix-4 digits put its recurrence within\n  0.03 ns of the worst path's reported arrival. The stalled CoreMark trace\n  retired 93,960 MULs and zero high-half multiplies, divides or remainders\n  between the markers. A registered M-extension lane can break both timing\n  paths if the low-half multiply costs just one extra cycle.\nhypothesis: |\n  Use the existing blocking divider issue and completion boundary for all\n  RV32M operations. Route a finished result from the registered M-extension\n  datapath into EX/MEM while ordinary integer and address operations still\n  take one EX cycle. Shorten the divider recurrence inside that lane so it\n  can run at the clock gained by isolating multiplication.\n\n  On multiply launch, use forwarded operands to register four products of\n  16-bit limbs. Give each limb a 17th bit, zero for low limbs and either\n  zero or the sign bit for each high limb as required by the operation. Let\n  P00 be the low-low product, P11 the high-high product, and M the signed\n  34-bit sum of the two cross products and zero-extended P00[31:16]. Form M\n  with carry-save compression followed by one carry-propagate addition.\n  MUL advances into EX/MEM on the next edge with {M[15:0], P00[15:0]},\n  incurring one extra EX cycle. The high-half variants take another edge\n  to register the sign-extended M[33:16], then add it to P11 modulo 2^32\n  as they advance. This places a register between the DSP outputs and the\n  wide EX/MEM re\n…[2551 of 5623 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:fcdc4623bbc70a5f]…\nast integer ALU and retain its RV32I behavior.\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: Extend the existing EX wait to both M-extension units, capture their forwarded source operands at launch for RVFI, and select the ready result on valid advance.\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: Retain all integer vectors and migrate every multiply vector to the clocked multiplier test.\n  - file: test/test_mul_unit.py\n    description: Exercise all four products against exact bit results, including limb-carry boundaries, mixed signs, signed extrema, variant latency, reset and a held result.\n  - file: test/test_div_unit.py\n    description: Preserve all divider vectors and fixed-latency checks and cover the first trial with every two-bit dividend prefix and divisor zero through four.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: Add the multiplier source and cover forwarded inputs, multiply followed by dependent divide, an older store held by dmem, and a squashed wrong-path multiply with contiguous RVFI order.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'set -e\nscratch=/srv/hwebench/tmp/4876824c/8a23b80d/bench-r3s1.9yfM6wt8\npython3 - \"$scratch/cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\" <<'\"'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport sys\np = Path(sys.argv[1]); s = p.read_text(); pos = s.index('def test_pipeline_runner():')\ns = s[:pos] + '''@cocotb.test()\nasync def multiply_divide_and_squash_with_backpressure(dut):\n    product = _r(1, 2, 1, 0, 3, 0b0110011)\n    wrong_path = _r(1, 4, 4, 0, 4, 0b0110011)\n    program = [\n        ADDI(2, 0, 7),\n        LW(1, 0, 0),\n        SW(2, 0, 4),\n        product,\n        DIV(4, 3, 2),\n        BEQ(0, 0, 8),\n        wrong_path,\n        SW(4, 0, 8),\n        EBREAK(),\n    ]\n    bus = []\n    rets, dmem = await _run(dut, program, {0: 100}, dmem_stalls={4: 3},\n                            imem_stalls={28: 2}, bus_trace=bus)\n    assert [r['pc'] for r in rets] == [0, 4, 8, 12, 16, 20, 28, 32]\n    assert [r['order'] for r in rets] == list(range(8))\n    assert all(r['trap'] == 0 for r in rets)\n    product_retirement, quotient_retirement = rets[3:5]\n    assert product_retirement['rs1_rdata'] == 100\n    assert product_retirement['rs2_rdata'] == 7\n    assert product_retirement['rd_wdata'] == 700\n    assert product_retirement['cycle'] - rets[2]['cycle'] == 2\n    assert quotient_retirement['rs1_rdata'] == 700\n    assert quotient_retirement['rd_wdata'] == 100\n    assert quotient_retirement['cycle'] - product_retirement['cycle'] == 9\n    assert dmem == {0: 100, 4: 7, 8: 100}\n    assert [addr for _, addr, wen in bus if wen] == [4, 4, 4, 4, 8]\n\n\n''' + s[pos:]\np.write_text(s)\nPY\ncd \\\"\"'$scratch\"\npytest -q --rootdir=\"$scratch\" -o cache_dir=\"$scratch/pytest_cache\" cores/bench/test > \"$scratch/m_cocotb.log\" 2>&1\ntail -n 8 \"$scratch/m_cocotb.log\"'","aggregated_output":".......                                                                  [100%]\n7 passed in 18.39s