{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg '\\\"category\\\"\\\\s*:\\\\s*\\\"structural\\\"|hyp-20261120-001-r4s0' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python -c 'import json,sys; rows=[json.loads(s) for s in sys.stdin]; print(\\\"fields\\\",list(rows[-1])); [print(json.dumps({k:v for k,v in r.items() if k not in (\\\"changes\\\", \\\"commit\\\")},indent=2)) for r in rows]'\"", "aggregated_output": "fields ['id', 'title', 'category', 'motivation', 'hypothesis', 'expected_impact', 'changes', 'outcome', 'fitness', 'delta_pct', 'vs_baseline', 'fmax_mhz', 'ipc_coremark', 'cycles', 'iterations', 'lut4', 'ff', 'seeds', 'perturbations', 'lutram', 'bsram', 'dsp', 'critical_path', 'logic_levels', 'formal_passed', 'cosim_passed', 'error', 'implementation_notes', 'timestamp', 'slot', 'round_id', 'lesson']\n{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20261120-002-r1s1\",\n  \"title\": \"Shared multicycle RV32M divider\",\n  \"category\": \"structural\",\n  \"motivation\": \"The Gowin baseline reaches 5.442 MHz and 12.12 CoreMark iter/sec. Its\\n199.837 ns worst path spans 156 cells from MEM/WB through forwarding and the\\nEX ALU. The variable signed and unsigned division and remainder expressions\\nare the likely source of that depth. They feed the shared ALU result used for\\ndata addresses, so their timing cost applies even when CoreMark is executing\\na load, store, or integer instruction. The baseline Verilator trace under\\nthe scored stall settings retired zero DIV, DIVU, REM, or REMU instructions\\nin the 4,491,485-cycle marked CoreMark window. The run passed the canonical\\nCRC checks.\\n\",\n  \"hypothesis\": {\n    \"motivation\": \"The Gowin baseline reaches 5.442 MHz and 12.12 CoreMark iter/sec. Its\\n199.837 ns worst path spans 156 cells from MEM/WB through forwarding and the\\nEX ALU. The variable signed and unsigned division and remainder expressions\\nare the likely source of that depth. They feed the shared ALU result used for\\ndata addresses, so their timing cost applies even when CoreMark is executing\\na load, store, or integer instruction. The baseline Verilator trace under\\nthe scored stall settings retired zero DIV, DIVU, REM, or REMU instructions\\nin the 4,491,485-cycle marked CoreMark window. The run passed the canonical\\nCRC checks.\\n\",\n    \"hypothesis\": \"Move DIV, DIVU, REM, and REMU onto one registered restoring divider. Capture\\nunsigned operand magnitudes and sign flags at launch. Reuse six cascaded\\nradix-2 steps per cycle for six cycles, shifting in a 3\n…[40932 of 44004 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:81598bc4d17c9031]…\nS checks on the final RTL with zero failures and zero retries. Cocotb and ISS cosim exercised the real divider arithmetic.\\n- All 79 cocotb cases across seven runners passed, including the directed divider and pipeline regressions.\\n- Self-test RVFI cosim passed against the ISS in zero-wait and stalled modes. Stalled CoreMark passed all five canonical CRCs, emitted `Correct operation validated.`, and completed without out-of-bounds accesses. The start and stop markers were at cycles 15,168 and 4,328,689.\\n\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-20T04:18:09.903364Z\",\n  \"slot\": 1,\n  \"round_id\": 4,\n  \"lesson\": \"- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-002-r4s1 (regression, +10.78%): Registering the raw JALR adder sum as the load/store address exposed predictor-write and divider paths, so staging table writes and replacing cascaded radix-8 steps with one parallel radix-16 digit shifted the limit to EX, where parallel result selection and next-PC comparisons raised median Gowin Fmax from 61.366 to 66.022 MHz at unchanged CoreMark cycles.\"\n}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
