{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_45","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg '\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20261120-002-r7s1\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python -c 'import json,sys;x=json.load(sys.stdin);print(x[\\\"hypothesis\\\"])'\"","aggregated_output":"{'motivation': 'The champion scores 192.85 CoreMark iterations per second over 4,015,275\\nmarked cycles at 77.436 MHz. Two of its three Gowin placements are\\ndivider-limited. The divider computes two dependent digits on the prefix\\nedge and uses fifteen wide trial subtractors on each subsequent edge.\\nCoreMark retires no divisions or remainders in the measured window, so\\nshortening the divider paths can raise fitness at the same cycle count.\\nThe earlier magnitude split in r5s1 cascaded two narrower digit steps.\\nA single digit on each work edge removes that serial dependency.\\n', 'hypothesis': 'Use one setup edge and six single-digit edges. Select the lane on\\nrequest capture from the unsigned divisor magnitude D. For nonzero D\\nbelow 2^14, set up the quotient and remainder from the top two\\ndividend bits. Only D equal to 1, 2 or 3 can affect that prefix.\\nRegister the 19-bit odd multiples through 31D on the same setup edge.\\nUse shifts and a single add, subtract or carry-save sum for each odd\\nmultiple. Derive even multiples by shifting the registered odd values.\\nThen consume five dividend bits per edge. Subtract the digit multiples\\nin parallel from the 19-bit trial {remainder, next_bits}. Select the\\nlargest fitting digit and its residual using adjacent borrow flags and\\nan OR of one-hot masked residuals. The remainder is less than D and\\nfits in 14 bits.\\n\\nFor D at or above 2^14, the top 14 dividend bits already fit in the\\nremainder and the corresponding quotient bits are zero. Seed that\\nremainder at setup while preparing the wide odd multiples through 7D,\\nthen consume the remaining 18 bits in six radix-8 steps with seven\\nparallel trial subtracts. The remainder before a wide digit is bounded\\nby the consumed dividend prefix, which is at most 29 bits before the\\nfinal digit. Form a 32-bit trial and reject a candidate if its 35-bit\\nmultiple has nonzero upper bits or its 32-bit subtract borrows.\\nKeep separate remainder registers and share the 32-bit shift register\\nthat replaces consumed dividend bits with quotient bits.\\n\\nRetain the current blocking EX handshake and eight-edge\\nrequest-to-transfer schedule in real and ALTOPS modes. Complete and\\nhold the result even if EX cannot accept it. For divisor zero, retain\\nthe captured dividend magnitude and return the original signed or\\nunsigned dividend for remainder, or all ones for quotient. Preserve\\nsigned correction and INT_MIN divided by -1 behavior.\\n\\nA scratch implementation reached 86.306, 82.433 and 82.433 MHz in the\\nthree Gowin placements with 5,493 logic cells. The cocotb suites and ISS\\nco-simulation passed, and stalled CoreMark validated the canonical CRCs\\nin 4,015,275 marked cycles. The median gives 205.30 iter/sec, up 6.45%\\nfrom 192.85 iter/sec. EX operand-to-result and recovery paths now limit\\nthe measured placements. At these cycles the 4.6% acceptance threshold\\nrequires a median above about 81.0 MHz.\\n', 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 6, 'confidence': 'medium'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/div_unit.sv', 'description': 'Implement the two radix schedules, bounded remainder lanes and matched real and ALTOPS completion timing.'}, {'file': 'test/test_div_unit.py', 'description': 'Cover signed and unsigned cases around the magnitude split, maximal digits, zero and overflow, and stable completion under result backpressure.'}]}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
