\nCapture the selected hash alongside the next request PC on each fetch\\nacceptance and hold both on a stall. The registered index removes the\\nhash from the RAM read path.\\n\\nCapture the selected full-width EX correction address independently of\\nmispredict and hold it during a pending redirect. Bypass the predictor\\nfor the first corrected instruction and predict that instruction's PC+4\\nand its hash. This keeps the recovery address mux out of the predictor\\nfeedback path. Use the selected successor for both fetch advance and\\nthe synchronous replay read. The corrected instructi\n…[21153 of 24225 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:cb8de5244e164d6b]…\ne M requests on a registered late miss.'}, {'file': 'rtl/mem_stage.sv', 'description': 'Validate the late branch with the registered load or the saved fallback value, suppress younger bus effects and retirement on annulment, and report actual operands, traps and successors.'}, {'file': 'rtl/if_stage.sv', 'description': 'Predecode the bus and replay words, carry the bit through the queue, arbitrate registered recovery and training, and hold the older correction through backpressure.'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Verify dependent branch forwarding, taken and fall-through rollback with stalls, FENCE.I, and cancellation of a younger store or divide.'}]}, 'fmax_mhz': 86.39, 'ipc_coremark': 3e-06, 'cycles': 3357185, 'lutram': 161, 'bsram': 6, 'critical_path': {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/u_div/dividend_quotient_q_30_s1', 'to': 'cpu/u_ex/u_div/partial_remainder_q_4_s0', 'slack_ns': -6.479, 'arrival_ns': 16.773, 'logic_cells': 41, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex/u_div']}, 'implementation_notes': ''}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
