{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'COREMARK_SIZE|COREMARK_OPT|ITERATIONS' tools/eval/fpga.py bench/programs/coremark/baremetal/core_portme.h; sed -n '249,315p' test/cosim/main.cpp; git status --short --untracked-files=all\"","aggregated_output":"bench/programs/coremark/baremetal/core_portme.h:5:/* ITERATIONS=10 matches VexRiscv's regression default. With our cosim's\nbench/programs/coremark/baremetal/core_portme.h:10:#ifndef ITERATIONS\nbench/programs/coremark/baremetal/core_portme.h:11:#define ITERATIONS    10\nbench/programs/coremark/baremetal/core_portme.h:16: * the default in upstream coremark.h. Pass COREMARK_SIZE=2000 to the\ntools/eval/fpga.py:60:# -O3, ITERATIONS=10. Verified against VexRiscv's pre-compiled\ntools/eval/fpga.py:84:    \"\"\"Read ITERATIONS from portme.h so we can't get out of sync with the ELF.\"\"\"\ntools/eval/fpga.py:87:        raise RuntimeError(f\"{path} not found — can't determine CoreMark ITERATIONS\")\ntools/eval/fpga.py:88:    m = re.search(r'^\\s*#\\s*define\\s+ITERATIONS\\s+(\\d+)', path.read_text(), re.MULTILINE)\ntools/eval/fpga.py:90:        raise RuntimeError(f\"ITERATIONS not found in {path}\")\ntools/eval/fpga.py:211:    # 50M cycle ceiling: 2K CoreMark with ITERATIONS=10 + iStall+dStall\n                 top->io_rvfi_mode_1, top->io_rvfi_ixl_1)) break;\n#endif\n    }\n    if (bench_mode) {\n        // Emit final record, plus an explicit completion marker. Consumers MUST\n        // check \"ebreak\":true before trusting the cycle count — otherwise the\n        // benchmark hit maxcycles without completing and the reading is invalid.\n        if (bench_last[0]) puts(bench_last);\n        // Escape backslash/quote/newline in uart_buf for JSON string safety.\n        std::string esc;\n        for (char c : uart_buf) {\n            if (c == '\\\\' || c == '\"') { esc.push_back('\\\\'); esc.push_back(c); }\n            else if (c == '\\n') { esc += \"\\\\n\"; }\n            else if (c == '\\r') { esc += \"\\\\r\"; }\n            else if (c == '\\t') { esc += \"\\\\t\"; }\n            else if (c >= 0x20 && c < 0x7F) { esc.push_back(c); }\n            // drop other non-printables silently\n        }\n        printf(\"{\\\"ebreak\\\":%s,\\\"maxcycles_hit\\\":%s,\\\"oob\\\":%s,\"\n               \"\\\"bench_start_cycle\\\":%llu,\\\"bench_stop_cycle\\\":%llu,\"\n               \"\\\"bench_bracketed\\\":%s,\\\"uart\\\":\\\"%s\\\"}\\n\",\n               hit_ebreak ? \"true\" : \"false\",\n               hit_ebreak ? \"false\" : \"true\",\n               oob_access ? \"true\" : \"false\",\n               (unsigned long long)bench_start_cycle,\n               (unsigned long long)bench_stop_cycle,\n               (bench_start_set && bench_stop_set) ? \"true\" : \"false\",\n               esc.c_str());\n    }\n    delete top;\n    // Non-zero exit if sim ran out of cycles OR an out-of-bounds memory\n    // access occurred. OOB historically silently aliased to dmem[0] which\n    // could mask CPU effective-address bugs — now it fails loud.\n    if (!hit_ebreak) return 2;\n    if (oob_access)  return 3;\n    return 0;\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg 'hyp-20261120-001-r10s0|hyp-20261120-002-r10s1' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import json,sys; [print(r[\\\"id\\\"],r[\\\"hypothesis\\\"],r.get(\\\"implementation_notes\\\")) for r in map(json.loads,sys.stdin)]'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_21", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg 'hyp-20261120-001-r10s0|hyp-20261120-002-r10s1' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import json,sys; [print(r[\\\"id\\\"],r[\\\"hypothesis\\\"],r.get(\\\"implementation_notes\\\")) for r in map(json.loads,sys.stdin)]'\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261120-001-r10s0 {'motivation': 'The round 9 late BEQ/BNE lane cut marked CoreMark cycles from\\n3,540,112 to 3,402,673. Its 84.28 MHz median left the score just below\\nthe acceptance threshold. A fresh stalled trace of the champion\\nreproduced its cycle count and CRCs. All 135,320 adjacent load-dependent\\nBEQ/BNE retirements in the interval used a byte or halfword load, or\\ncompared a word load to x0. A width-aware lane can cover those cases\\nwith at most 16 bits of late comparison. Adjacent load-to-store data\\ndependencies occurred only 420 times in the same trace.\\n', 'hypothesis': \"Remove the adjacent load-use bubble for a validated BEQ or BNE when\\nthe producer is a byte or halfword load, the other source is x0, or\\nboth branch sources match the producer. Keep the existing interlock\\nfor full-width comparisons against an arbitrary register and for\\nother EX consumers. Qualify the EX/MEM load forwarding tag with a\\nnaturally aligned, side-effecting load and a nonzero destination.\\nA trapping load leaves the branch resolving normally with the older\\narchitectural value. An unready load holds the branch in EX through\\nthe existing dmem stall.\\n\\nCompute a load-zero flag in parallel with MEM load formatting, then\\nregister it alongside the load result. Reduce each byte of the raw\\nresponse independently and combine the flags for the selected lanes.\\nThis works for signed and unsigned loads because extension preserves\\nzero. In EX, capture the other forwarded operand's low 16 bits and\\nwhether its upper 16 bits equal the extension of its own bit 15\\nrequired by the load's signedness. The formatted load's bit 15 is\\nthe sign bit for a signed byte or halfword. In MEM, compare the low\\n16 bits and use the saved upper check, the registered zero flag, or\\nthe always-equal case when both source tags match. Keep the full\\noperand values for RVFI.\\n\\nIn EX, capture full-width matches of fall-through and target against\\nthe oldest unissued PC and fold alignment and BEQ/BNE polarity into\\nthe two possible mismatch bit\n…[13622 of 16694 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:917490f97e8206a0]…\ncosim TARGET=bench NRET=1` matched the ISS selftest with and without stalls and validated the CoreMark CRCs. Directed cases cover address carry and wraparound, ineligible and trapping producers, subword equality, late recovery, wrong-path effects, and contiguous retirement.\n- Canonical stalled CoreMark completed ten iterations in 3,343,491 marked cycles, a 5.55% reduction from 3,540,112 cycles. At this cycle count, the throughput target requires about 82.906 MHz median Gowin Fmax.\n- Gowin synthesis inferred six block RAMs, with two for instruction replay and four for the FPGA data memory. Median placement timing is pending.\n- The unchanged single-channel formal suite was incomplete locally. On the submitted RTL, 43 of 53 checks had passed at the last poll, including liveness, both PC consistency checks, uniqueness, illegal instructions, and causal ordering. Register consistency was still running. Earlier RTL revisions reached 52 of 53. No run produced a counterexample, and there were no formal-driven fixes.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
