 first correction cycle. Keep the\\nregistered correction PC stable until imem accepts it,\\nand keep EX squashed until decode accepts the first corrected instruction.\\nA ready correction can still issue immediately or enqueue through a dmem\\nhold. Use PC+4 as the corrected instruction's speculative successor.\\n\\nAdd one bit to each trained target row that records whether its target\\nand source share replay row PC[10:2]. Compute it from the staged training\\naddresses beside the target hash. The prediction still supplies the next\\nPC and launches its synchronous replay read. Whe\n…[14983 of 18055 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:b3fd91a68f4b1ab1]…\nent to the existing in-order pipeline controls.'}, {'file': 'rtl/if_stage.sv', 'description': 'Predecode the eligible consumer class. Register retry separately from backend annulment, suppress failed training and hold retry through backpressure.'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Cover a branch whose guessed word differs while equality matches, an equality mismatch, a load-address mismatch, chained speculation, producer faults, and bus holds during retry.'}]} 7 [81.752, 88.703, 88.703] [[0, 81.752, 11], [1, 88.703, 14], [2, 88.703, 14]]\n128:def _run_gw_sh(outdir: Path, log: Path, env: dict) -> bool:\n133:        proc = subprocess.Popen([str(GOWIN_HOME / \"IDE/bin/gw_sh\"), \"build.tcl\"], cwd=outdir,\n158:    timed_out = _run_gw_sh(outdir, log, gowin_env(env, outdir))\n52:sim_build/\n54:test/cosim/sim_build/\n55:test/**/sim_build/\n63:# Bench ELFs (rebuild from sources)\n64:bench/programs/*.elf\n69:# Held-out benchmark ELFs (rebuild via `make -f bench/holdout/Makefile all`)\n70:bench/holdout/build/*.elf\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
