he registered D. The radix-4 recurrence yields the required divide-by-zero values with quotient negation suppressed. The signed overflow case falls out of the normal 32-bit result selection. Divider vectors moved to a dedicated cocotb runner. The pipeline regression checks that a divide captures a load result across a stalled older store and forwards its quotient immediately to the next instruction.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Verilator `-Wall` lint passed for both the hardware and ALTOPS builds. The guarded\n…[1207 of 4279 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:40489c55c247917b]…\neline's 156-cell worst path through the ALU. Fitness increased 730.2%. The stalled CoreMark trace recorded two DIVU retirements outside the markers and zero DIV or REM family retirements in the measured interval. Divide-heavy workloads pay the eight additional EX cycles per operation.\n\n\nid hyp-20261120-002-r1s1\nfitness 97.34\nfmax_mhz 43.722\ncycles 4491485\nlut4 2773\nff 566\ncritical_path {'from': 'cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_id/id_ex_w.rs2_val_0_s100', 'slack_ns': -19.52, 'arrival_ns': 29.814, 'logic_cells': 52, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_if', 'cpu/u_hazard', 'cpu/u_id']}\nseeds [40.783, 43.722, 43.722]\nimplementation_notes \n\nid hyp-20261120-003-r1s2\nfitness 13.14\nfmax_mhz 5.546\ncycles 4220145\nlut4 12446\nff 521\ncritical_path {'from': 'cpu/u_ex/reg_q.rd_2_s0', 'to': 'dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -192.449, 'arrival_ns': 202.744, 'logic_cells': 158, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\nseeds [5.065, 5.546, 5.546]\nimplementation_notes \n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
