on every valid EX advance, including for non-control instructions so a stale entry can never let a wrong-path instruction issue. Correct mismatches ahead of all fetch holds and squash the younger fetch-to-ID slot. Preserve the existing trap fall-through, link value, and resolved successor reported by RVFI. On a correct prediction, accept the younger instruction subject to normal hazards and imem readiness.\\n\\nA temporary implementation reduced marker-bracketed CoreMark cycles with both bus stalls from 4,491,485 to 4,220,145 and produced all canonical CRCs. \n…[23654 of 26726 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:fd426d581023ab33]…\n\n- All seven cocotb runners passed. The 20 pipeline cases include FIFO refill and drain under stalls, a queued load-use hazard, a trained jump fetched during a multiply hold, and correction after a data stall filled the FIFO.\n- ISS co-simulation passed selftest and all three random programs with and without combined bus stalls. Stalled CoreMark matched the canonical CRCs and validation string and completed the ten marker-bracketed iterations in 4,015,275 cycles.\n- `make fpga TARGET=bench NRET=1` measured 56.324, 59.793, and 59.793 MHz for Gowin placement options 0, 1, and 2. Option 0 used 4,620 LUT4s and 1,273 registers. The median yields 148.91 CoreMark iterations per second, 7.78% above the 138.16 baseline. The cycle count matches the prototype. Median frequency was 2.180 MHz below the prototype.\n\n\n\n{'from': 'cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s', 'to': 'dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s', 'slack_ns': -12.755, 'arrival_ns': 23.049, 'logic_cells': 23, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_ex/u_alu', 'cpu/u_ex']}\n\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
