{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg 'hyp-20261120-003-r[1-5]s2|hyp-20261120-001-r5s0' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import sys,json\nfor line in sys.stdin:\n x=json.loads(line)\n print(x[\\\"id\\\"],x[\\\"category\\\"],x[\\\"fitness\\\"],x[\\\"fmax_mhz\\\"],x[\\\"cycles\\\"],x[\\\"lut4\\\"])\n print((x.get(\\\"implementation_notes\\\") or \\\"\\\")[-6400:])\n if x[\\\"id\\\"].endswith(\\\"r5s2\\\"): print(x[\\\"hypothesis\\\"][\\\"hypothesis\\\"])'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg 'hyp-20261120-003-r[1-5]s2|hyp-20261120-001-r5s0' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import sys,json\nfor line in sys.stdin:\n x=json.loads(line)\n print(x[\\\"id\\\"],x[\\\"category\\\"],x[\\\"fitness\\\"],x[\\\"fmax_mhz\\\"],x[\\\"cycles\\\"],x[\\\"lut4\\\"])\n print((x.get(\\\"implementation_notes\\\") or \\\"\\\")[-6400:])\n if x[\\\"id\\\"].endswith(\\\"r5s2\\\"): print(x[\\\"hypothesis\\\"][\\\"hypothesis\\\"])'\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261120-003-r1s2 predictor 13.14 5.546 4220145 12446\n\nhyp-20261120-003-r2s2 predictor 117.93 49.767 4220145 3714\n# Registered branch predictor recovery\n\nIF uses a 64-entry direct-mapped last-successor table with a full PC tag, a word-aligned successor, and separate resettable valid bits. EX trains the table on each advancing, non-trapping control transfer, including a conditional fall-through.\n\nEX compares the sequential and control successors with the fetch PC in parallel with branch direction. IF captures the resolved address whenever recovery is inactive, independently of the mismatch decision. A registered mismatch selects the captured address and annuls the younger EX slot until the target is accepted. On acceptance, fetch advances using the target instruction's prediction.\n\nDecode receives raw instruction data. Fetch acceptance records ID/EX validity, and effective EX validity gates load-use detection, memory operations, forwarding writes, divider requests, table training, and retirement. The implementation removes the old IF/ID flush and the unused EX/MEM branch metadata. RVFI remains single-retirement and reports the resolved successor.\n\nThe directed tests verify a trained JALR hit, a changed target held through three imem stall cycles, and the absence of wrong-path store requests. A second test replaces a trained JAL with a load and verifies that recovery holds through dmem backpressure and annuls a wrong-path divide.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator lint passed without warnings.\n- Single-retirement ALTOPS formal passed all 53 checks on the first run.\n- All six cocotb runners passed.\n- ISS co-simulation passed selftest and all three random traces with and without both bus stalls. CoreMark passed the canonical CRC check with 4,220,145 marker-bracketed cycles under both stalls.\n- `make fpga TARGET=bench` scored 117.93 iterations/sec, above the 105.22 threshold. Gowin placement options 0, 1, and 2 reached 45.530, 49.767, and 49.767 MHz. Option 0 used 3,714 LUT4s and its longest reported path crossed\n…[10263 of 13335 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:1c48feaa6d60f59f]…\nthe head. Preserve trap, link,\nmemory side effects, RVFI successors and single retirement.\n\nA scratch prototype completed canonical stalled CoreMark in 3,972,442\nmarked cycles, 7.91% below the 4,313,521-cycle champion. A page-local\nlast-successor table feeding the same queue took 4,013,625 cycles.\nGowin placement options 0, 1, and 2 measured 63.024, 67.033, and\n67.033 MHz for the hysteretic design. The median yields 168.75 iter/sec,\n10.04% above the 153.35 iter/sec champion. At that cycle count the\n4.6% acceptance margin requires about 63.72 MHz.\nOption 0 used 4,632 LUT4s and 88 LUT RAM cells. ISS selftest and all\nthree random traces passed with zero-wait and stalled buses. All 81\ncocotb cases passed after adapting two exact fetch schedules and adding\ndirected tests for full refill and drain, cross-page correction from\na full queue to DIV, and direction hysteresis. The unchanged\nsingle-retire formal run passed 52 checks, including liveness and PC\ncontinuity. The register consistency check was still running.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
