{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,230p' tools/eval/gowin.py && ls -la /srv/hwebench/toolchain && git log -6 --oneline && rg --files cores/bench/rtl\"", "aggregated_output": "\"\"\"Vendor place-and-route and timing for the FPGA fitness (HWE Bench V2).\n\nV2 times designs with Gowin EDA (the FPGA vendor's own synthesis, place and\nroute and static timing analysis) instead of Yosys + nextpnr, whose timing\nmodel for this part misses whole classes of paths. The vendor flow is also\ndeterministic and insensitive to circuit-neutral netlist changes.\n\nFmax is the median over Gowin's placement algorithms (PLACE_OPTIONS), each\na full build of the same RTL; results are deterministic for a given input.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor\nimport os\nimport re\nimport shutil\nimport statistics\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom tools.eval._subprocess import remove_path\n\nGOWIN_HOME = Path(os.environ.get(\"GOWIN_HOME\", \"/opt/gowin\"))\nGOWIN_VERSION = \"1.9.11.03 Education\"\nPART = \"GW2AR-LV18QN88C8/I7\"      # Tang Nano 20K\nDEVICE_VERSION = \"C\"\nPLACE_OPTIONS = (0, 1, 2)\nCST = \"fpga/constraints/Tang_Nano_20K.cst\"\nSDC = \"fpga/constraints/clock.sdc\"\nSTALL_GEN = \"fpga/bench_stall_gen.sv\"\nBUILD_TIMEOUT_SEC = 2700\n\n\ndef gowin_env(base: dict | None, workdir: Path) -> dict:\n    env = dict(os.environ if base is None else base)\n    libs = [GOWIN_HOME / \"deps/root/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu\", GOWIN_HOME / \"IDE/lib\"]\n    env[\"LD_LIBRARY_PATH\"] = \":\".join(map(str, libs))\n    env[\"QT_QPA_PLATFORM\"] = \"offscreen\"\n    xdg = workdir / \".xdg\"\n    xdg.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    os.chmod(xdg, 0o700)\n    env[\"XDG_RUNTIME_DIR\"] = str(xdg)\n    return env\n\n\ndef rtl_sources(rtl_dir: Path) -> list[Path]:\n    srcs = sorted(rtl_dir.glob(\"*.sv\"))\n    pkg = rtl_dir / \"core_pkg.sv\"\n    return ([pkg] if pkg in srcs else []) + [p for p in srcs if p != pkg]\n\n\ndef project_tcl(worktree: Path, rtl_dir: Path, bench_sv: str, place_option: int) -> str:\n    files = [*rtl_sources(rtl_dir), worktree / STALL_GEN, worktree / bench_sv,\n             worktree / CST, worktree / SDC]\n    return \"\\n\".join([\n        f\"set_device {PART} -device_version {DEVICE_VERSION}\",\n        *(f\"add_file {f}\" for f in fi\n…[8059 of 11131 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:508c2af390d6f525]…\nand all(not r[\"placement_failed\"] for r in res):\n        print(f\"score Fmax (median): {summarize(res)['fmax_mhz']} MHz\")\n    return 0 if all(not r[\"placement_failed\"] for r in res) else 1\n\n\nlrwxrwxrwx 1 nobody nogroup 18 Sep 28 02:57 /srv/hwebench/toolchain -> /opt/hwe-toolchain\n6df4e0f log: hyp-20261120-003-r5s2 regression\n4fdf841 log: hyp-20261120-002-r5s1 regression\n82b457c log: hyp-20261120-001-r5s0 improvement\n810eef5 hyp-20261120-001-r5s0: Shorten the arithmetic paths into memory and forwarding (+11.9%)\na49f632 log: hyp-20261120-003-r4s2 regression\n9e420bf log: hyp-20261120-002-r4s1 regression\ncores/bench/rtl/mul_unit.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/decoder.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/forward_unit.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/imm_gen.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/alu.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/reg_file.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/hazard_unit.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/id_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/div_unit.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/wb_stage.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/core.sv\ncores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg -i 'predictor|fetch buffer' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import sys,json\nfor line in sys.stdin:\n x=json.loads(line)\n print(x[\\\"id\\\"], x[\\\"title\\\"], x[\\\"fmax_mhz\\\"], x[\\\"cycles\\\"], x[\\\"fitness\\\"], x[\\\"lut4\\\"], x[\\\"ff\\\"])\n if x[\\\"id\\\"].endswith(\\\"r2s1\\\"):\n  print(x[\\\"hypothesis\\\"][\\\"hypothesis\\\"])\n if x[\\\"id\\\"].endswith(\\\"r5s2\\\"):\n  print(type(x.get(\\\"implementation_notes\\\")), str(x.get(\\\"implementation_notes\\\"))[:100])'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_11", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -i 'predictor|fetch buffer' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import sys,json\nfor line in sys.stdin:\n x=json.loads(line)\n print(x[\\\"id\\\"], x[\\\"title\\\"], x[\\\"fmax_mhz\\\"], x[\\\"cycles\\\"], x[\\\"fitness\\\"], x[\\\"lut4\\\"], x[\\\"ff\\\"])\n if x[\\\"id\\\"].endswith(\\\"r2s1\\\"):\n  print(x[\\\"hypothesis\\\"][\\\"hypothesis\\\"])\n if x[\\\"id\\\"].endswith(\\\"r5s2\\\"):\n  print(type(x.get(\\\"implementation_notes\\\")), str(x.get(\\\"implementation_notes\\\"))[:100])'\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261120-003-r1s2 Predict fetch with a tagged last-next-PC table 5.546 4220145 13.14 12446 521\nhyp-20261120-002-r2s1 Decouple instruction fetch with an elastic buffer 49.878 4353657 114.57 3059 697\nReplace the combinational IF/ID interface with a one-entry fall-through\nbuffer for the fetched instruction and its PC. Decode sees the stored\npayload when the buffer is full and the raw bus payload otherwise. Select\nthe payload using only the registered full bit. Drive decode availability\nfrom buffer-full or imemReady. Wire the selected instruction directly to\nthe decoder and register-file read addresses. Let the wide ID/EX payload\nsample whenever EX can take a new entry, including when ID/EX marks the\nentry invalid. Apply redirect, fetch availability and load-use to the\nID/EX valid bit. This cuts the redirect-to-decode datapath while retaining\none instruction per clock with both buses ready.\n\nOn an empty buffer, bypass a ready fetch into decode or save it if decode\nis blocked. A full buffer may drain and refill on the same edge. Increment\nthe fetch PC only on an accepted fetch, with the PC and word recorded\ntogether. Allow an empty slot to fill during load-use, divider or data-bus\nbackpressure. Keep a same-cycle EX redirect when the valid, aligned\ncontrol-flow instruction advances into EX/MEM. Give it priority over\nenqueue, dequeue and sequential PC advance. Invalidate the buffer and\nID/EX's next entry and install the target in the fetch PC on that edge.\nThe target can bypass to decode on the next ready cycle. A branch held\nbehind a stalled data request must redirect only on its advance.\n\nPreserve the load-use bubble, held operands, same-cycle writeback bypass,\nand the divider's handshake and latency. Preserve the existing handling\nof misaligned control-flow targets and accepted data-memory transactions.\nQualify divider start, redirect, destination writes and memory requests\nwith the originating instruction's validity. Preserve forwarding of a\npreviously retired MEM/WB result to an instruction held by a data stall.\nRetire in order through the single-channel RVFI interface and use the\nexisting formal and cosim gates.\n\nExpect the wide redirect-to-ID path to disappear from the Gowin report.\nThe buffer can use an instruction-bus ready cycle during a backend hold\nand then supply decode on an instruction-bus stall.\nAt unchanged marked cycles a median above 47.26 MHz clears the champion\nthreshold and about 52 MHz yields the forecast gain. Compare placement\nmedians and stalled CoreMark marker counts separately, since the buffer\nadds a decode input mux and the remaining EX and divider paths can limit\nthe clock.\n\nhyp-20261120-003-r2s2 Register branch predictor recovery before squashing execute 49.767 4220145 117.93 3714 724\nhyp-20261120-003-r3s2 Run a compact next-PC predictor ahead of decode 49.663 4008388 123.9 3846 728\nhyp-20261120-002-r4s1 Separate execute paths for memory and branch prediction 66.022 4313521 153.06 4837 980\nhyp-20261120-003-r4s2 Run the successor predictor ahead through a shift FIFO 59.793 4015275 148.91 4620 1273\nhyp-20261120-001-r5s0 Shorten the arithmetic paths into memory and forwarding 74.008 4313521 171.57 4894 890\nhyp-20261120-002-r5s1 Split divider feedback by divisor magnitude 72.226 4313521 167.44 4295 766\nhyp-20261120-003-r5s2 Run a hysteretic branch predictor ahead through a LUT RAM queue 66.933 3972442 168.49 4667 1142\n<class 'str'> \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
