{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'predictor|r7s2|r6s2|r5s2' cores/bench/LESSONS.md schemas/hypothesis.schema.json; ls -la cores/bench/experiments\"","aggregated_output":"schemas/hypothesis.schema.json:8:    \"category\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"micro_opt\",\"structural\",\"extension\",\"predictor\",\"memory\"]},\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:5:- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-003-r2s2 (improvement, +17.24%): Registering the next-PC mismatch and capturing the resolved target independently cuts the EX-to-ID redirect path, while annulling the younger EX slot as the target enters ID/EX keeps misses to one bubble, letting the tagged successor predictor cut stalled CoreMark cycles by 6.04% as median Gowin Fmax rises from 45.180 to 49.767 MHz.\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:8:- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-003-r3s2 (regression, +5.06%): A two-entry fall-through queue let the tagged next-PC predictor fetch through load-use bubbles and data-bus holds, cutting stalled CoreMark cycles by 5.02%, with a median Gowin Fmax of 49.663 MHz against the 55.38 MHz needed at that cycle count to match the round-winning RV32M lane.\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:10:- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-002-r4s1 (regression, +10.78%): Registering the raw JALR adder sum as the load/store address exposed predictor-write and divider paths, so staging table writes and replacing cascaded radix-8 steps with one parallel radix-16 digit shifted the limit to EX, where parallel result selection and next-PC comparisons raised median Gowin Fmax from 61.366 to 66.022 MHz at unchanged CoreMark cycles.\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:13:- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-002-r5s1 (regression, +9.19%): Bounding the remainder to 12 bits for divisor magnitudes below 4096 and skipping 12 leading zero quotient bits at or above 4096 removes the cascaded full-width radix-8 steps within the eight-edge transfer schedule, shifting Gowin's critical path to EX forwarding into the predictor and capping the CoreMark gain at 9.19%.\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:14:- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-003-r5s2 (regression, +9.87%): A page-local predictor with two-bit direction counters feeding a LUT RAM fetch queue cut stalled CoreMark cycles by 7.91%, with the divider’s divisor-to-remainder path capping median Gowin Fmax at 66.933 MHz and leaving it short of the 68.16 MHz needed to match the round winner at that cycle count.\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:17:- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-003-r6s2 (regression, +6.88%): Bypassing the registered decode head into ID/EX on ready redirects avoids a refill cycle before division and preserves retirement liveness, while the divider capped median Gowin Fmax at 73.253 MHz, a large enough clock deficit against the four-entry fall-through queue to outweigh the lower stalled CoreMark cycle count.\ncores/bench/LESSONS.md:20:- 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-003-r7s2 (improvement, +9.39%): Replaying learned BTB successor words during instruction-bus stalls cut CoreMark cycles by 6.39%, and writing every accepted word into a FIFO slot free at cycle start, even on decode bypass, removed decode acceptance from the RAM write enable and helped reach 79.292 MHz median Gowin Fmax.\ntotal 300\ndrwxrwx---+ 3 nobody nogroup   4096 Nov 20 09:11 .\ndrwxrwx---+ 5 nobody nogroup   4096 Nov 20 09:11 ..\n-rw-rw----+ 1 nobody nogroup      0 Nov 20 09:11 .gitkeep\ndrwxrwx---+ 2 nobody nogroup   4096 Nov 20 09:11 hypotheses\n-rw-rw----+ 1 nobody nogroup 205394 Nov 20 09:11 log.jsonl\n-rw-rw----+ 1 nobody nogroup  71503 Nov 20 09:11 progress.png\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
