dentity via the hashed index and tag. On a valid\\nunconditional hit or a conditional hit with counter MSB set, reconstruct\\nthe target from the source page and stored offset. Otherwise use full-width\\nPC+4. Clear the indexed target-valid bit on cross-page training. Use a\\nseparate two-bit saturating direction table at the same index. Treat its\\nfirst update after reset as starting from weakly not taken. Allow aliases\\nin the direction counters while still requiring a full target hit.\\n\\nRegister advancing EX training packets before committing table writes.\\nTrain on legal, non-squashed control transfers with an aligned target.\\nFor a conditional branch, record its taken targ\n…[32033 of 35105 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:10b148dd892b4e74]…\non at its marked cycle count.\n- The replay storage grew option 0 to 7,539 logic cells and 1,104 registers. EX recovery is on the longest path, with the divider close on options 1 and 2.\n- Local formal was incomplete within the wall-clock budget. The unchanged `formal/run_all.sh` gate reported 14 of 53 checks passing on the selected RTL, including illegal-instruction trapping, order uniqueness, liveness, and both PC checks. Zero failures or counterexamples were reported. Bitwuzla spent substantially longer unrolling the registered queue discard design, and the register consistency check was still solving.\n\ntimestamp 2026-11-20T08:09:48.351227Z\nslot 2\nround_id 7\nlesson - 2026-11-20 hyp-20261120-003-r7s2 (improvement, +9.39%): Replaying learned BTB successor words during instruction-bus stalls cut CoreMark cycles by 6.39%, and writing every accepted word into a FIFO slot free at cycle start, even on decode bypass, removed decode acceptance from the RAM write enable and helped reach 79.292 MHz median Gowin Fmax.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
